            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1929. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/concatenation-of-array\\\">1929. Concatenation of Array</a></b></span>\\n<div>Create an array by concatenating a given array with itself.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given an integer array `nums` of length `n`.<br/>2. Create an array `ans` of length `2n`, where for each index `i` (0 ≤ `i` ＜ `n`), `ans[i]` and `ans[i + n]` are equal to `nums[i]`.<br/>3. Essentially, `ans` is formed by concatenating `nums` with itself.<br/>4. Return the array `ans`.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>[1,3,2,1] => [1,3,2,1,1,3,2,1]</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,2,1]<br/>Output: [1,2,1,1,2,1]<br/>Explanation: The array ans is formed as follows:<br/>- ans = [nums[0],nums[1],nums[2],nums[0],nums[1],nums[2]]<br/>- ans = [1,2,1,1,2,1]<br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,3,2,1]<br/>Output: [1,3,2,1,1,3,2,1]<br/>Explanation: The array ans is formed as follows:<br/>- ans = [nums[0],nums[1],nums[2],nums[3],nums[0],nums[1],nums[2],nums[3]]<br/>- ans = [1,3,2,1,1,3,2,1]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>n == nums.length<br/>1 <= n <= 1000<br/>1 <= nums[i] <= 1000<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/concatenation-of-array/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/concatenation-of-array/solutions/1369400/javascript-one-liner/\\\">Array Concatenation</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>- No additional setup required.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>return [<br/>        ...nums,<br/>        ...nums<br/>    ];</div>\\n<div>1. Use the spread operator to concatenate `nums` with itself.<br/>2. Return the resulting array.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution uses the spread operator to concatenate the given array `nums` with itself, creating a new array of double the length with repeated elements.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative approach using Array.concat<br/>\\n    var getConcatenationAlt = function(nums) {<br/>\\n        return nums.concat(nums);<br/>\\n    };<br/><br/>\\n    This alternative solution uses the `concat` method to concatenate the array `nums` with itself, achieving the same result in a slightly different way.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>O(n), where n is the length of the array `nums`.</div>\"}",
