            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1512. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-good-pairs\\\">1512. Number of Good Pairs</a></b></span>\\n<div>Count the number of 'good pairs' in an array.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given an integer array `nums`.<br/>2. A pair (i, j) is considered 'good' if `nums[i] == nums[j]` and `i ＜ j`.<br/>3. The task is to return the number of good pairs in the array.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>[1,1,1,1] => 6</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,2,3,1,1,3]<br/>Output: 4<br/>Explanation: There are 4 good pairs (0,3), (0,4), (3,4), (2,5) 0-indexed.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,1,1,1]<br/>Output: 6<br/>Explanation: Each pair in the array are good.<br/><br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,2,3]<br/>Output: 0<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= nums.length <= 100<br/>1 <= nums[i] <= 100<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-good-pairs/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\",\"media\":[]}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-good-pairs/solutions/911686/clean-javascript-solution/\\\">Hash Map</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Setup: Define initial variables<br/>\\n    let nums = [1,2,3,1,1,3]; // Example nums array<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    // Main Solution Code: Using hash map<br/>\\n    const map = {};<br/>\\n    let count = 0;<br/>\\n    for (const number of nums) {<br/>\\n        if (map[number]) {<br/>\\n            count += map[number];<br/>\\n            map[number] += 1;<br/>\\n        } else {<br/>\\n            map[number] = 1;<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n    return count;<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize a hash map to store the frequency of each number in `nums`.<br/>2. Iterate through each number in `nums`.<br/>3. For each number, if it exists in the hash map, increment the count of good pairs by the frequency of that number.<br/>4. Increase the frequency of that number in the hash map.<br/>5. Return the count of good pairs.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the logic and approach<br/>\\n    The solution uses a hash map to efficiently count the number of occurrences of each number. It then calculates the number of good pairs based on these frequencies.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Using nested loops (Time Complexity: O(n^2))<br/>\\n    function numIdenticalPairsAlt(nums) {<br/>\\n        let count = 0;<br/>\\n        for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {<br/>\\n            for (let j = i + 1; j < nums.length; j++) {<br/>\\n                if (nums[i] === nums[j]) {<br/>\\n                    count++;<br/>\\n                }<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        return count;<br/>\\n    }<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>- O(n), where n is the length of the array `nums`.</div>\",\"media\":[]}",
