            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1637. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/widest-vertical-area-between-two-points-containing-no-points\\\">1637. Widest Vertical Area Between Two Points Containing No Points</a></b></span>\\n<div>Find the widest vertical area between points on a 2D plane.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given `n` points on a 2D plane, where `points[i] = [xi, yi]`.<br/>2. The task is to find the widest vertical area between two points where no points lie within the area.<br/>3. A vertical area extends infinitely along the y-axis and has a fixed width.<br/>4. Points on the edge of a vertical area are not considered inside the area.<br/>5. The widest vertical area is the one with the maximum width.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>[[3,1],[9,0],[1,0],[1,4],[5,3],[8,8]] => 3</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>​<br/>Input: points = [[8,7],[9,9],[7,4],[9,7]]<br/>Output: 1<br/>Explanation: Both the red and the blue area are optimal.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: points = [[3,1],[9,0],[1,0],[1,4],[5,3],[8,8]]<br/>Output: 3<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>n == points.length<br/>2 <= n <= 105<br/>points[i].length == 2<br/>0 <= xi, yi <= 109<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/widest-vertical-area-between-two-points-containing-no-points/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\",\"media\":[]}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/widest-vertical-area-between-two-points-containing-no-points/solutions/1728684/beginner-friendly-javascript-solution/\\\">Sorting</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Setup: Define initial variables<br/>\\n    let points = [[8,7],[9,9],[7,4],[9,7]]; // Example points array<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    // Main Solution Code: Using sorting and iteration<br/>\\n    points.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);<br/>\\n    let max = 0;<br/>\\n    for(let i = 0; i < points.length - 1; i++) {<br/>\\n        max = Math.max(max, points[i + 1][0] - points[i][0]);<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n    return max;<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Sort the points array based on the x-coordinate.<br/>2. Initialize a variable `max` to keep track of the maximum width found.<br/>3. Iterate through the sorted array, comparing the x-coordinate of adjacent points.<br/>4. Calculate the width of each vertical area (difference in x-coordinates) and update `max` if the current width is larger.<br/>5. Return the value of `max`.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the logic and approach<br/>\\n    The solution involves sorting the points by their x-coordinates and then iterating through them to find the maximum width of the vertical area that can be formed between adjacent points.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Using reduce for a more compact approach<br/>\\n    function maxWidthOfVerticalAreaAlt(points) {<br/>\\n        return points<br/>\\n            .sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0])<br/>\\n            .reduce((max, point, i, arr) => (i > 0) ? Math.max(max, point[0] - arr[i-1][0]) : max, 0);<br/>\\n    }<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>- O(n*logn), due to the sorting of points.</div>\",\"media\":[]}",
