            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2011. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/final-value-of-variable-after-performing-operations\\\">2011. Final Value of Variable After Performing Operations</a></b></span>\\n<div>Calculate the final value of a variable after performing a list of increment and decrement operations.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. A programming language has only four operations: `++X`, `X++`, `--X`, and `X--`.<br/>2. These operations respectively increment or decrement the value of a variable `X` by 1.<br/>3. Initially, `X` is 0.<br/>4. Given an array `operations` containing a list of these operations, determine the final value of `X`.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>[\\\"--X\\\",\\\"X++\\\",\\\"X++\\\"] => 1</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: operations = [\\\"--X\\\",\\\"X++\\\",\\\"X++\\\"]<br/>Output: 1<br/>Explanation: The operations are performed as follows:<br/>Initially, X = 0.<br/>--X: X is decremented by 1, X =  0 - 1 = -1.<br/>X++: X is incremented by 1, X = -1 + 1 =  0.<br/>X++: X is incremented by 1, X =  0 + 1 =  1.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: operations = [\\\"++X\\\",\\\"++X\\\",\\\"X++\\\"]<br/>Output: 3<br/>Explanation: The operations are performed as follows:<br/>Initially, X = 0.<br/>++X: X is incremented by 1, X = 0 + 1 = 1.<br/>++X: X is incremented by 1, X = 1 + 1 = 2.<br/>X++: X is incremented by 1, X = 2 + 1 = 3.<br/><br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: operations = [\\\"X++\\\",\\\"++X\\\",\\\"--X\\\",\\\"X--\\\"]<br/>Output: 0<br/>Explanation: The operations are performed as follows:<br/>Initially, X = 0.<br/>X++: X is incremented by 1, X = 0 + 1 = 1.<br/>++X: X is incremented by 1, X = 1 + 1 = 2.<br/>--X: X is decremented by 1, X = 2 - 1 = 1.<br/>X--: X is decremented by 1, X = 1 - 1 = 0.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= operations.length <= 100<br/>operations[i] will be either \\\"++X\\\", \\\"X++\\\", \\\"--X\\\", or \\\"X--\\\".<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/final-value-of-variable-after-performing-operations/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/final-value-of-variable-after-performing-operations/solutions/1520355/javascript-one-line-solution-time-81-mem-92-w-documentation/\\\">Array Reduction</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Setup: Define initial variables<br/>\\n    let operations = [\\\"--X\\\",\\\"X++\\\",\\\"X++\\\"]; // Example operations array<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    // Main Solution Code: Using reduce method<br/>\\n    operations.reduce((acc, curr) => {<br/>\\n        return curr[1] === \\\"+\\\" ? ++acc : --acc;<br/>\\n    }, 0);<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Use the `reduce` method on the `operations` array.<br/>2. For each operation, check if it includes an increment (`+`) or decrement (`-`).<br/>3. Increment or decrement the accumulator (`acc`) accordingly.<br/>4. The initial value of the accumulator is 0.<br/>5. Return the final value of the accumulator.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the logic and approach<br/>\\n    The solution uses the `reduce` method to iterate over each operation in the `operations` array, adjusting the value of `X` based on whether the operation is an increment or a decrement.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Using a for loop<br/>\\n    function finalValueAfterOperationsAlt(operations) {<br/>\\n        let x = 0;<br/>\\n        for (let operation of operations) {<br/>\\n            if (operation.includes('+')) {<br/>\\n                x++;<br/>\\n            } else {<br/>\\n                x--;<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        return x;<br/>\\n    }<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>- O(n), where n is the number of operations in the `operations` array.</div>\"}",
