            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2433. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/find-the-original-array-of-prefix-xor\\\">2433. Find The Original Array of Prefix Xor</a></b></span>\\n<div>Reconstruct an array based on its XOR prefix sums.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given an integer array `pref` of size `n`.<br/>2. The goal is to find an array `arr` of the same size such that `pref[i] = arr[0] ^ arr[1] ^ ... ^ arr[i]` for every `i`.<br/>3. The bitwise XOR operation is denoted by `^`.<br/>4. It is guaranteed that the solution is unique.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>[5,2,0,3,1] => [5,7,2,3,2]</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: pref = [5,2,0,3,1]<br/>Output: [5,7,2,3,2]<br/>Explanation: From the array [5,7,2,3,2] we have the following:<br/>- pref[0] = 5.<br/>- pref[1] = 5 ^ 7 = 2.<br/>- pref[2] = 5 ^ 7 ^ 2 = 0.<br/>- pref[3] = 5 ^ 7 ^ 2 ^ 3 = 3.<br/>- pref[4] = 5 ^ 7 ^ 2 ^ 3 ^ 2 = 1.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: pref = [13]<br/>Output: [13]<br/>Explanation: We have pref[0] = arr[0] = 13.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= pref.length <= 105<br/>0 <= pref[i] <= 106<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/find-the-original-array-of-prefix-xor/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/find-the-original-array-of-prefix-xor/solutions/2682898/easy/\\\">Bitwise XOR</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Setup: Define initial variables<br/>\\n    let pref = [5,2,7,3]; // Example prefix XOR array<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    // Main Solution Code: Reconstructing array using bitwise XOR<br/>\\n    let arr = [];<br/>\\n    arr[0] = pref[0];<br/>\\n    for (let i = 1; i < pref.length; i++) {<br/>\\n        arr[i] = pref[i] ^ pref[i - 1];<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n    return arr;<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize an array `arr` with the same size as `pref`.<br/>2. Set `arr[0]` equal to `pref[0]`.<br/>3. Iterate over `pref` from index 1.<br/>4. For each index `i`, calculate `arr[i]` by performing XOR operation `pref[i] ^ pref[i-1]`.<br/>5. Return the array `arr`.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the logic and approach<br/>\\n    The solution leverages the property of XOR where `a ^ b ^ b = a` to reconstruct each element of the original array from its prefix XOR sums.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Using map for a more concise solution<br/>\\n   return pref.map((value, index) => index === 0 ? value : value ^ pref[index - 1]);<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>- O(n), where n is the length of the array `pref`.</div>\"}",
