            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1470. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/shuffle-the-array\\\">1470. Shuffle the Array</a></b></span>\\n<div>Rearrange an array of `2n` elements from `[x1, x2, ..., xn, y1, y2, ..., yn]` to `[x1, y1, x2, y2, ..., xn, yn]`.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given an array `nums` containing `2n` elements in the form `[x1, x2, ..., xn, y1, y2, ..., yn]`.<br/>2. The task is to rearrange the elements to the form `[x1, y1, x2, y2, ..., xn, yn]`.<br/>3. It is guaranteed that the array contains `2n` elements.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>[1,2,3,4,4,3,2,1], 4 => [1,4,2,3,3,2,4,1]</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [2,5,1,3,4,7], n = 3<br/>Output: [2,3,5,4,1,7] <br/>Explanation: Since x1=2, x2=5, x3=1, y1=3, y2=4, y3=7 then the answer is [2,3,5,4,1,7].<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,2,3,4,4,3,2,1], n = 4<br/>Output: [1,4,2,3,3,2,4,1]<br/><br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,1,2,2], n = 2<br/>Output: [1,2,1,2]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= n <= 500<br/>nums.length == 2n<br/>1 <= nums[i] <= 10^3<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/shuffle-the-array/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\",\"media\":[]}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/shuffle-the-array/solutions/675956/in-place-o-n-time-o-1-space-with-explanation-analysis/\\\">In-place rearrangement with bit manipulation.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Setup: Define initial variables<br/>\\n    let nums = [2,5,1,3,4,7]; // Example array<br/>\\n    let n = 3; // Midpoint of the array<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    // Main Solution Code: In-place rearrangement with bit manipulation<br/>\\n    let i = n - 1;<br/>\\n    for (let j = nums.length - 1; j >= n; j--) {<br/>\\n        nums[j] <<= 10;<br/>\\n        nums[j] |= nums[i];<br/>\\n        i--;<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n    i = 0;<br/>\\n    for (let j = n; j < nums.length; j++) {<br/>\\n        const num1 = nums[j] & 1023;<br/>\\n        const num2 = nums[j] >> 10;<br/>\\n        nums[i] = num1;<br/>\\n        nums[i + 1] = num2;<br/>\\n        i += 2;<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n    return nums;<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Iterate backward through the second half of the array (`nums`).<br/>2. Use two pointers, `i` for the first half and `j` for the second half.<br/>3. Store both `nums[i]` and `nums[j]` in `nums[j]` using bit manipulation.<br/>4. In a second loop, extract these pairs and place them in their final position.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the logic and approach<br/>\\n    The solution combines pairs of elements in the array using bit manipulation, then decodes them back into their required order.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Iterative approach without bit manipulation<br/>\\n    function shuffleAlt(nums, n) {<br/>\\n        let result = [];<br/>\\n        for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {<br/>\\n            result.push(nums[i], nums[i + n]);<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        return result;<br/>\\n    }<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>- O(n), where n is the length of the given array.</div>\",\"media\":[]}",
