            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1282. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/group-the-people-given-the-group-size-they-belong-to\\\">1282. Group the People Given the Group Size They Belong To</a></b></span>\\n<div>Group people based on their group size preference.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You are given `n` people, each with a unique ID from 0 to `n - 1`.<br/>2. An integer array `groupSizes` is provided, where `groupSizes[i]` represents the preferred group size of person `i`.<br/>3. You must form groups such that each person `i` is in a group of size `groupSizes[i]`.<br/>4. Each person must be in exactly one group.<br/>5. The task is to return a list of groups meeting these conditions.<br/>6. Multiple valid solutions may exist; any one of them is acceptable.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>[2,1,3,3,3,2] => [[1],[0,5],[2,3,4]]</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: groupSizes = [3,3,3,3,3,1,3]<br/>Output: [[5],[0,1,2],[3,4,6]]<br/>Explanation: <br/>The first group is [5]. The size is 1, and groupSizes[5] = 1.<br/>The second group is [0,1,2]. The size is 3, and groupSizes[0] = groupSizes[1] = groupSizes[2] = 3.<br/>The third group is [3,4,6]. The size is 3, and groupSizes[3] = groupSizes[4] = groupSizes[6] = 3.<br/>Other possible solutions are [[2,1,6],[5],[0,4,3]] and [[5],[0,6,2],[4,3,1]].<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: groupSizes = [2,1,3,3,3,2]<br/>Output: [[1],[0,5],[2,3,4]]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>groupSizes.length == n<br/>1 <= n <= 500<br/>1 <= groupSizes[i] <= n<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/group-the-people-given-the-group-size-they-belong-to/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/group-the-people-given-the-group-size-they-belong-to/solutions/971536/simple-javascript-solution/\\\">Hash Table</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Setup: Define initial variables<br/>\\n    let groupSizes = [3,3,3,3,3,1,3]; // Example group sizes array<br/>\\n    let result = []; // An array to store the final groups<br/>\\n    let hash = {}; // A hash table to temporarily store groups<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    // Main Solution Code: Using hash table<br/>\\n    for (let i = 0; i ＜ groupSizes.length; i++) {<br/>\\n        const num = groupSizes[i];<br/>\\n        hash[num] ? hash[num].push(i) : hash[num] = [i];<br/>\\n        if (hash[num].length === num) {<br/>\\n            result.push(hash[num]);<br/>\\n            delete hash[num];<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Iterate over the `groupSizes` array.<br/>2. For each element, add the index to a hash table, grouping by the element value.<br/>3. Once a group reaches its desired size, add it to the result and remove it from the hash table.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the logic and approach<br/>\\n    The solution uses a hash table to gather members into groups based on their preferred size. When a group reaches its desired size, it is added to the result list.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Iterative approach with forEach<br/>\\n    function groupThePeople(groupSizes) {<br/>\\n        const groups = {};<br/>\\n        const result = [];<br/>\\n        groupSizes.forEach((size, index) => {<br/>\\n            if (!groups[size]) {<br/>\\n                groups[size] = [];<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n            groups[size].push(index);<br/>\\n            if (groups[size].length === size) {<br/>\\n                result.push(groups[size]);<br/>\\n                groups[size] = [];<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n        });<br/>\\n        return result;<br/>\\n    }<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>O(n), where n is the number of people.</div>\"}",
