            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2610. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/convert-an-array-into-a-2d-array-with-conditions\\\">2610. Convert an Array Into a 2D Array With Conditions</a></b></span>\\n<div>Create a 2D array from a given integer array such that each row contains distinct integers, and the number of rows is minimal.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You are given an integer array `nums`.<br/>2. Create a 2D array from `nums` with these conditions:<br/>   - All elements of `nums` must be used.<br/>   - Each row in the 2D array must contain distinct integers.<br/>   - Minimize the number of rows in the 2D array.<br/>3. You can return any valid 2D array that satisfies these conditions.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [nums = [1,3,4,1,2,3,1]] => [[1,3,4,2],[1,3],[1]]</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,3,4,1,2,3,1]<br/>Output: [[1,3,4,2],[1,3],[1]]<br/>Explanation: We can create a 2D array that contains the following rows:<br/>- 1,3,4,2<br/>- 1,3<br/>- 1<br/>All elements of nums were used, and each row of the 2D array contains distinct integers, so it is a valid answer.<br/>It can be shown that we cannot have less than 3 rows in a valid array.<br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,2,3,4]<br/>Output: [[4,3,2,1]]<br/>Explanation: All elements of the array are distinct, so we can keep all of them in the first row of the 2D array.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= nums.length <= 200<br/>1 <= nums[i] <= nums.length<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XxBW71n-9FA&pp=ygU2MjYxMC4gQ29udmVydCBhbiBBcnJheSBJbnRvIGEgMkQgQXJyYXkgV2l0aCBDb25kaXRpb25z\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=effm-Mt4jz0&pp=ygVAMjYxMC4gQ29udmVydCBhbiBBcnJheSBJbnRvIGEgMkQgQXJyYXkgV2l0aCBDb25kaXRpb25zamF2YXNjcmlwdA%3D%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/convert-an-array-into-a-2d-array-with-conditions/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/convert-an-array-into-a-2d-array-with-conditions/solutions/4489692/simple-javascript-solution/\\\">- Algorithm: Frequency Counting and 2D Array Construction</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>```javascript<br/>var findMatrix = function(nums) {<br/>    const res = [];   // To store the resulting 2D array<br/>    const freq = {};  // To keep track of the frequency of each element<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>var findMatrix = function(nums) {<br/>    const res = [],<br/>        freq = {};<br/>    for (let i = 0; i ＜ nums.length; i++) {<br/>        const n = nums[i],<br/>            numCount = (freq[n] || 0) + 1;<br/>        freq[n] = numCount;<br/>        if (!res[numCount - 1]) res[numCount - 1] = [n];<br/>        else res[numCount - 1].push(n);        <br/>    return res;<br/>};</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize an empty array `res` to store the 2D array and an object `freq` to keep track of frequencies.<br/>2. Iterate through each element in `nums`.<br/>3. For each element, update its frequency in `freq`.<br/>4. Determine which row the current element should be placed in the 2D array based on its frequency.<br/>5. If the row does not exist, create it. Otherwise, add the element to the existing row.<br/>6. Continue until all elements are placed.<br/>7. Return the resulting 2D array `res`.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution involves counting the frequency of each element in `nums` and placing each element in a row of the 2D array based on its frequency. The goal is to ensure each row has distinct elements while minimizing the number of rows. This is achieved by dynamically creating new rows in the 2D array as needed when an element's frequency increases.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n), where n is the number of elements in `nums`. This complexity arises from iterating through the array once.</div>\"}",
