            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2006. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-number-of-pairs-with-absolute-difference-k\\\">2006. Count Number of Pairs With Absolute Difference K</a></b></span>\\n<div>Count the number of pairs in an array with an absolute difference equal to a given value.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given an integer array `nums` and an integer `k`.<br/>2. Task: Find the number of pairs `(i, j)` in `nums` where `i ＜ j` and `|nums[i] - nums[j]| == k`.<br/>3. `|x|` is the absolute value of `x`.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [nums = [1,2,2,1], k = 1] => 4</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,2,2,1], k = 1<br/>Output: 4<br/>Explanation: The pairs with an absolute difference of 1 are:<br/>- [1,2,2,1]<br/>- [1,2,2,1]<br/>- [1,2,2,1]<br/>- [1,2,2,1]<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,3], k = 3<br/>Output: 0<br/>Explanation: There are no pairs with an absolute difference of 3.<br/><br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [3,2,1,5,4], k = 2<br/>Output: 3<br/>Explanation: The pairs with an absolute difference of 2 are:<br/>- [3,2,1,5,4]<br/>- [3,2,1,5,4]<br/>- [3,2,1,5,4]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= nums.length <= 200<br/>1 <= nums[i] <= 100<br/>1 <= k <= 99<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=noP_AsQlgQc&pp=ygU2MjAwNi4gQ291bnQgTnVtYmVyIG9mIFBhaXJzIFdpdGggQWJzb2x1dGUgRGlmZmVyZW5jZSBL\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8fLeNeGtFqc&pp=ygVAMjAwNi4gQ291bnQgTnVtYmVyIG9mIFBhaXJzIFdpdGggQWJzb2x1dGUgRGlmZmVyZW5jZSBLamF2YXNjcmlwdA%3D%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-number-of-pairs-with-absolute-difference-k/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-number-of-pairs-with-absolute-difference-k/solutions/1480690/simple-javascript-solution/\\\">- Algorithm: Frequency Counting and Pair Matching</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>```javascript<br/>var countKDifference = function(nums, k) {<br/>    let map = {}; // To store the frequency of each number<br/>    let pairs = 0; // To count the pairs<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>```javascript<br/>var countKDifference = function(nums, k) {<br/>    let map = {};<br/>    for(let i of nums) {<br/>        map[i] ? map[i]++ : map[i] = 1;</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize a map `map` to store the frequency of each number in `nums`.<br/>2. Iterate through `nums` to populate `map`.<br/>3. Initialize a variable `pairs` to count the number of valid pairs.<br/>4. Iterate through `nums` again.<br/>5. For each element, check if `map[nums[i] - k]` exists.<br/>6. If it exists, increment `pairs` by the value of `map[nums[i] - k]`.<br/>7. Return the count of `pairs`.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution uses a frequency map to count the occurrences of each number. Then, it iterates through the array again, checking for each element if there exists a corresponding element (difference equals `k`) in the map. If it exists, it adds the frequency of this corresponding element to the total pairs count.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n), where n is the number of elements in `nums`. This is due to two separate passes through the array.</div>\"}",
