            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1732. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/find-the-highest-altitude\\\">1732. Find the Highest Altitude</a></b></span>\\n<div>Find the highest altitude reached in a biker's road trip, given the net altitude gains at each point.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. The biker starts at an altitude of 0.<br/>2. Each element in the `gain` array represents the net altitude change from one point to the next.<br/>3. Calculate the altitude at each point and return the maximum altitude reached.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [gain = [-5,1,5,0,-7]] => 1</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: gain = [-5,1,5,0,-7]<br/>Output: 1<br/>Explanation: The altitudes are [0,-5,-4,1,1,-6]. The highest is 1.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: gain = [-4,-3,-2,-1,4,3,2]<br/>Output: 0<br/>Explanation: The altitudes are [0,-4,-7,-9,-10,-6,-3,-1]. The highest is 0.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>n == gain.length<br/>1 <= n <= 100<br/>-100 <= gain[i] <= 100<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dx2ecjEVQZM&pp=ygUfMTczMi4gRmluZCB0aGUgSGlnaGVzdCBBbHRpdHVkZQ%3D%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dx2ecjEVQZM&pp=ygUpMTczMi4gRmluZCB0aGUgSGlnaGVzdCBBbHRpdHVkZWphdmFzY3JpcHQ%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/find-the-highest-altitude/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/find-the-highest-altitude/solutions/2480590/javascript-less-than-86-85-and-faster-than-91-23/\\\">- Algorithm: Iterative Altitude Calculation</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>```javascript<br/>const largestAltitude = gain => {<br/>    let previous = 0; // Initial altitude<br/>    let biggest = 0;  // Maximum altitude<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>```javascript<br/>const largestAltitude = gain => {    <br/>    let previous = 0;<br/>    let biggest = 0;</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize `previous` altitude to 0 (starting altitude).<br/>2. Initialize `biggest` altitude to 0 (highest altitude reached).<br/>3. Iterate through the `gain` array.<br/>4. Add the current gain to `previous` to get the current altitude.<br/>5. If the current altitude is greater than `biggest`, update `biggest`.<br/>6. Return `biggest` after completing the iteration.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution involves iterating through the `gain` array to calculate the altitude at each point. The maximum altitude is tracked and updated as the iteration progresses.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n), where n is the length of the `gain` array. This is due to a single pass through the array.</div>\"}",
