            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1672. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/richest-customer-wealth\\\">1672. Richest Customer Wealth</a></b></span>\\n<div>Determine the maximum wealth among all customers based on their bank accounts.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You are provided with a 2D integer grid `accounts`, representing various customers' money in different banks.<br/>2. `accounts[i][j]` is the amount of money the ith customer has in the jth bank.<br/>3. A customer's wealth is the sum of all money they have in their bank accounts.<br/>4. The task is to find and return the wealth of the richest customer.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>[ [1,5],[7,3],[3,5] ] => 10</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: accounts = [[1,2,3],[3,2,1]]<br/>Output: 6<br/>Explanation:<br/>1st customer has wealth = 1 + 2 + 3 = 6<br/>2nd customer has wealth = 3 + 2 + 1 = 6<br/>Both customers are considered the richest with a wealth of 6 each, so return 6.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: accounts = [[1,5],[7,3],[3,5]]<br/>Output: 10<br/>Explanation: <br/>1st customer has wealth = 6<br/>2nd customer has wealth = 10 <br/>3rd customer has wealth = 8<br/>The 2nd customer is the richest with a wealth of 10.<br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: accounts = [[2,8,7],[7,1,3],[1,9,5]]<br/>Output: 17<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>m == accounts.length<br/>n == accounts[i].length<br/>1 <= m, n <= 50<br/>1 <= accounts[i][j] <= 100<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/richest-customer-wealth/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/richest-customer-wealth/solutions/1035457/javascript-1-line-solution/\\\">Array Manipulation and Reduction</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>- No additional setup beyond the provided `accounts` array.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>1. Map each customer's accounts to the sum of their wealth.<br/>2. Use the spread operator to apply all customer wealth sums to `Math.max`.<br/>3. Return the maximum value found.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution involves mapping each customer's accounts to their total wealth and then finding the maximum wealth among all customers using `Math.max`.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>\\n    // Code: Finding the richest customer<br/>\\n    return Math.max(<br/>\\n      ...accounts.map(<br/>\\n        customer => customer.reduce((a, b) => a + b)<br/>\\n      )<br/>\\n    );<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Iterative approach<br/>\\n    function maximumWealth(accounts) {<br/>\\n        let maxWealth = 0;<br/>\\n        for (let account of accounts) {<br/>\\n            const wealth = account.reduce((sum, bank) => sum + bank, 0);<br/>\\n            maxWealth = Math.max(maxWealth, wealth);<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        return maxWealth;<br/>\\n    }<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>- O(m*n), where m is the number of customers and n is the number of banks.</div>\"}",
