            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2391. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-amount-of-time-to-collect-garbage\\\">2391. Minimum Amount of Time to Collect Garbage</a></b></span>\\n<div>Determine the minimum time required to collect all types of garbage from a series of houses, considering travel time between houses and the constraint of using only one garbage truck at a time.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You are given an array `garbage`, where each element is a string representing the garbage at each house, composed of 'M' (metal), 'P' (paper), and 'G' (glass).<br/>2. You are also given an array `travel`, where `travel[i]` represents the time to travel from house `i` to house `i+1`.<br/>3. There are three garbage trucks, each for a specific type of garbage. They start at house 0 and can skip houses but must follow the order.<br/>4. Only one truck can operate at a time, either driving or collecting garbage.<br/>5. The task is to calculate the minimum total time to collect all the garbage.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>Example: [\\\"G\\\",\\\"P\\\",\\\"GP\\\",\\\"GG\\\"], [2,4,3] => 21</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: garbage = [\\\"G\\\",\\\"P\\\",\\\"GP\\\",\\\"GG\\\"], travel = [2,4,3]<br/>Output: 21<br/>Explanation:<br/>The paper garbage truck:<br/>1. Travels from house 0 to house 1<br/>2. Collects the paper garbage at house 1<br/>3. Travels from house 1 to house 2<br/>4. Collects the paper garbage at house 2<br/>Altogether, it takes 8 minutes to pick up all the paper garbage.<br/>The glass garbage truck:<br/>1. Collects the glass garbage at house 0<br/>2. Travels from house 0 to house 1<br/>3. Travels from house 1 to house 2<br/>4. Collects the glass garbage at house 2<br/>5. Travels from house 2 to house 3<br/>6. Collects the glass garbage at house 3<br/>Altogether, it takes 13 minutes to pick up all the glass garbage.<br/>Since there is no metal garbage, we do not need to consider the metal garbage truck.<br/>Therefore, it takes a total of 8 + 13 = 21 minutes to collect all the garbage.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: garbage = [\\\"MMM\\\",\\\"PGM\\\",\\\"GP\\\"], travel = [3,10]<br/>Output: 37<br/>Explanation:<br/>The metal garbage truck takes 7 minutes to pick up all the metal garbage.<br/>The paper garbage truck takes 15 minutes to pick up all the paper garbage.<br/>The glass garbage truck takes 15 minutes to pick up all the glass garbage.<br/>It takes a total of 7 + 15 + 15 = 37 minutes to collect all the garbage.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>2 <= garbage.length <= 105<br/>garbage[i] consists of only the letters 'M', 'P', and 'G'.<br/>1 <= garbage[i].length <= 10<br/>travel.length == garbage.length - 1<br/>1 <= travel[i] <= 100<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-amount-of-time-to-collect-garbage/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-amount-of-time-to-collect-garbage/solutions/2593490/easy-javascript-solution-16-lines/\\\">Greedy Algorithm</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Setup: Initialize variables<br/>\\n    let garbage = ['G', 'P', 'M', 'GP', 'MG']; // Example garbage array<br/>\\n    let travel = [1, 2, 3, 4]; // Example travel times<br/>\\n    let travelTime = 0; // Initialize travel time<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    // Main Solution Code: Using greedy algorithm<br/>\\n    garbage = garbage.reverse();<br/>\\n    for (const type of ['G', 'P', 'M']) {<br/>\\n        const lastHouseWithGarbage = garbage.findIndex(house => house.includes(type));<br/>\\n        if (lastHouseWithGarbage !== -1) {<br/>\\n            travelTime += travel.slice(0, garbage.length - lastHouseWithGarbage - 1).reduce((acc, num) => acc + num, 0);<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Reverse the `garbage` array to start checking from the last house.<br/>2. Iterate over each type of garbage ('G', 'P', 'M').<br/>3. For each type, find the last house that contains that type of garbage.<br/>4. Calculate the travel time to that house by summing the travel times up to that house.<br/>5. If a garbage type is not present, skip to the next type.<br/>6. Sum the length of all garbage strings for collection time and add it to the total travel time.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the approach<br/>\\n    The solution finds the last house for each type of garbage and calculates the travel time to reach that house, then sums the collection times.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Different approach for the problem<br/>\\n    function minTimeToCollectGarbage(garbage, travel) {<br/>\\n        let travelTime = 0;<br/>\\n        let lastHouse = { 'G': -1, 'P': -1, 'M': -1 };<br/>\\n        for (let i = 0; i < garbage.length; i++) {<br/>\\n            for (const type of ['G', 'P', 'M']) {<br/>\\n                if (garbage[i].includes(type)) {<br/>\\n                    lastHouse[type] = i;<br/>\\n                }<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        for (const type in lastHouse) {<br/>\\n            if (lastHouse[type] !== -1) {<br/>\\n                travelTime += travel.slice(0, lastHouse[type]).reduce((acc, num) => acc + num, 0);<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        const collectionTime = garbage.reduce((acc, bin) => acc + bin.length, 0);<br/>\\n        return collectionTime + travelTime;<br/>\\n    }<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n), where n is the number of houses, as the solution iterates through each house once.<br/><br/></div>\"}",
