            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2859. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/sum-of-values-at-indices-with-k-set-bits\\\">2859. Sum of Values at Indices With K Set Bits</a></b></span>\\n<div>Find the sum of elements in an array where the indices of these elements have exactly 'k' set bits in their binary representation.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given a 0-indexed integer array `nums` and an integer `k`.<br/>2. You need to calculate the sum of those elements in `nums` for which the binary representation of their indices has exactly `k` set bits (1s).<br/>3. For example, if `k = 2`, sum the elements of `nums` whose indices have two set bits in their binary representation.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>Input: `nums = [4,3,2,1], k = 2` => Output: `1`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [5,10,1,5,2], k = 1<br/>Output: 13<br/>Explanation: The binary representation of the indices are: <br/>0 = 0002<br/>1 = 0012<br/>2 = 0102<br/>3 = 0112<br/>4 = 1002 <br/>Indices 1, 2, and 4 have k = 1 set bits in their binary representation.<br/>Hence, the answer is nums[1] + nums[2] + nums[4] = 13.<br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [4,3,2,1], k = 2<br/>Output: 1<br/>Explanation: The binary representation of the indices are:<br/>0 = 002<br/>1 = 012<br/>2 = 102<br/>3 = 112<br/>Only index 3 has k = 2 set bits in its binary representation.<br/>Hence, the answer is nums[3] = 1.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= nums.length <= 1000<br/>1 <= nums[i] <= 105<br/>0 <= k <= 10<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/sum-of-values-at-indices-with-k-set-bits/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/sum-of-values-at-indices-with-k-set-bits/solutions/4055060/javascript-2859-sum-of-values-at-indices-with-k-set-bits/\\\">The solution uses bitwise operations and iteration.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Setup: Define initial variables<br/>\\n    let a = [1, 2, 3, 4]; // Example array<br/>\\n    let k = 2; // Number of set bits<br/>\\n    let n = a.length; // Length of the array<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    // Main Solution Code: Using bitwise operations and iteration<br/>\\n    let sum = 0;<br/>\\n    for (let i = 0; i ＜ n; i++) {<br/>\\n        let setBits = i.toString(2).split('0').join('').length;<br/>\\n        if (setBits === k) {<br/>\\n            sum += a[i];<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize a variable to keep track of the sum.<br/>2. Iterate over each index of the array.<br/>3. For each index, convert the index to its binary representation.<br/>4. Count the number of set bits (1s) in the binary representation.<br/>5. If the count of set bits equals `k`, add the corresponding element from `nums` to the sum.<br/>6. Return the sum.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the logic and approach<br/>\\n    The function iterates through each index, converts it to binary, counts the set bits, and if they match `k`, adds the corresponding array value to the sum.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Using regex to count set bits<br/>\\n    function sumIndicesWithKSetBits(a, k) {<br/>\\n        let sum = 0;<br/>\\n        for (let i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {<br/>\\n            let setBits = i.toString(2).match(/1/g)?.length || 0;<br/>\\n            if (setBits === k) {<br/>\\n                sum += a[i];<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        return sum;<br/>\\n    }<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n * m), where n is the length of the array and m is the average number of bits for each index.<br/><br/></div>\"}",
