            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 807. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/max-increase-to-keep-city-skyline\\\">807. Max Increase to Keep City Skyline</a></b></span>\\n<div>Maximize the total increase in building heights in a city grid without altering the skyline from any cardinal direction.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You are given an `n x n` integer matrix `grid`, representing a city's layout where each cell contains a building's height.<br/>2. The task is to increase the height of any number of buildings without changing the city's skyline when viewed from the north, east, south, or west.<br/>3. The goal is to find the maximum total sum by which the building heights can be increased.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>Input: `grid = [[3,0,8,4],[2,4,5,7],[9,2,6,3],[0,3,1,0]]` => Output: `35`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: grid = [[3,0,8,4],[2,4,5,7],[9,2,6,3],[0,3,1,0]]<br/>Output: 35<br/>Explanation: The building heights are shown in the center of the above image.<br/>The skylines when viewed from each cardinal direction are drawn in red.<br/>The grid after increasing the height of buildings without affecting skylines is:<br/>gridNew = [ [8, 4, 8, 7],<br/>            [7, 4, 7, 7],<br/>            [9, 4, 8, 7],<br/>            [3, 3, 3, 3] ]<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: grid = [[0,0,0],[0,0,0],[0,0,0]]<br/>Output: 0<br/>Explanation: Increasing the height of any building will result in the skyline changing.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>n == grid.length<br/>n == grid[r].length<br/>2 <= n <= 50<br/>0 <= grid[r][c] <= 100<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/max-increase-to-keep-city-skyline/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/max-increase-to-keep-city-skyline/solutions/426489/clear-understandable-solution-using-map-and-meaningful-variables-90-speed-50-memory-o-n-2/\\\">The solution uses matrix manipulation and iteration.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Setup: Define initial variables<br/>\\n    let grid = [[3, 0, 8, 4], [2, 4, 5, 7], [9, 2, 6, 3], [0, 3, 1, 0]]; // Example grid<br/>\\n    let rowM = {}; // Object to store the maximum height of each row<br/>\\n    let colsM = {}; // Object to store the maximum height of each column<br/>\\n    let sum = 0; // Integer to accumulate the total height increase<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    // Main Solution Code: Using matrix manipulation<br/>\\n    for (let row = 0; row ＜ grid.length; row++) {<br/>\\n        for (let col = 0; col ＜ grid[0].length; col++) {<br/>\\n            let newH = Math.min(rowM[row], colsM[col]);<br/>\\n            if (grid[row][col] ＜ newH) {<br/>\\n                sum += newH - grid[row][col];<br/>\\n                grid[row][col] = newH;<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Create maps to store the maximum heights of each row and column.<br/>2. Iterate through the grid to populate these maps.<br/>3. Iterate again to calculate the maximum possible increase in height for each building without altering the skyline.<br/>4. Keep a running total of the height increases.<br/>5. Return the total sum of height increases.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the logic and approach<br/>\\n    The solution finds the maximum height that each building can be increased to without changing the skyline, sums these increases, and returns the total.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Using arrays to store max heights<br/>\\n    function maxIncreaseKeepingSkyline(grid) {<br/>\\n        let rowMaxes = new Array(grid.length).fill(0);<br/>\\n        let colMaxes = new Array(grid[0].length).fill(0);<br/>\\n        let sum = 0;<br/>\\n        for (let row = 0; row < grid.length; row++) {<br/>\\n            for (let col = 0; col < grid[0].length; col++) {<br/>\\n                rowMaxes[row] = Math.max(rowMaxes[row], grid[row][col]);<br/>\\n                colMaxes[col] = Math.max(colMaxes[col], grid[row][col]);<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        for (let row = 0; row < grid.length; row++) {<br/>\\n            for (let col = 0; col < grid[0].length; col++) {<br/>\\n                let newHeight = Math.min(rowMaxes[row], colMaxes[col]);<br/>\\n                sum += newHeight - grid[row][col];<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        return sum;<br/>\\n    }<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n^2), where n is the size of the grid.<br/><br/></div>\"}",
