            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1720. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/decode-xored-array\\\">1720. Decode XORed Array</a></b></span>\\n<div>Reconstruct a hidden array from its encoded XOR representation and a given first element.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. A hidden array `arr` of `n` non-negative integers is encoded into another array `encoded` of length `n - 1`, such that `encoded[i] = arr[i] XOR arr[i + 1]`.<br/>2. Given the `encoded` array and the first element of `arr` (`arr[0]`), the task is to return the original array `arr`.<br/>3. It's guaranteed that the solution exists and is unique.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>Input: `encoded = [1,2,3], first = 1` => Output: `[1,0,2,1]`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: encoded = [1,2,3], first = 1<br/>Output: [1,0,2,1]<br/>Explanation: If arr = [1,0,2,1], then first = 1 and encoded = [1 XOR 0, 0 XOR 2, 2 XOR 1] = [1,2,3]<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: encoded = [6,2,7,3], first = 4<br/>Output: [4,2,0,7,4]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>2 <= n <= 104<br/>encoded.length == n - 1<br/>0 <= encoded[i] <= 105<br/>0 <= first <= 105<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/decode-xored-array/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/decode-xored-array/solutions/1046860/simple-js-solution/\\\">XOR operation and array manipulation.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Setup: Initialize required variables<br/>\\n    let encoded = [1, 2, 3]; // Example encoded array<br/>\\n    let first = 1; // First element of the original array<br/>\\n    let arr = [first]; // Initialize arr with first element<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    // Code: Decoding the array using XOR operation<br/>\\n    for (let i = 0; i ＜ encoded.length; i++) {<br/>\\n        arr.push(arr[i] ^ encoded[i]);<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n    return arr;<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize an array `arr` with the first element of `arr`.<br/>2. Iterate through the `encoded` array.<br/>3. In each iteration, XOR the last element of `arr` with the current element of `encoded` and append the result to `arr`.<br/>4. Return the `arr` array as the decoded original array.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the logic and approach<br/>\\n    The solution leverages the property of XOR where `a XOR b = c` implies `a XOR c = b`. Starting with the first element, it sequentially decodes the original array.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Different approach to the problem<br/>\\n    const out = [first];<br/>\\n    encoded.forEach((x, i) => {<br/>\\n        out.push(out[i] ^ x);<br/>\\n    });<br/>\\n    return out;<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n), where n is the length of the `encoded` array.<br/><br/></div>\"}",
