            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2574. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/left-and-right-sum-differences\\\">2574. Left and Right Sum Differences</a></b></span>\\n<div>Find an array where each element is the absolute difference between the sum of elements to the left and right of that index in the given array.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given an integer array `nums`.<br/>2. Create an array `answer` where `answer[i]` is the absolute difference between the sum of elements to the left (`leftSum[i]`) and right (`rightSum[i]`) of index `i` in `nums`.<br/>3. If there are no elements to the left/right of `i`, `leftSum[i]`/`rightSum[i]` is considered 0.<br/>4. Return the `answer` array.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>Input: `nums = [10,4,8,3]` => Output: `[15,1,11,22]`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [10,4,8,3]<br/>Output: [15,1,11,22]<br/>Explanation: The array leftSum is [0,10,14,22] and the array rightSum is [15,11,3,0].<br/>The array answer is [|0 - 15|,|10 - 11|,|14 - 3|,|22 - 0|] = [15,1,11,22].<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1]<br/>Output: [0]<br/>Explanation: The array leftSum is [0] and the array rightSum is [0].<br/>The array answer is [|0 - 0|] = [0].<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= nums.length <= 1000<br/>1 <= nums[i] <= 105<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/left-and-right-sum-differences/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/left-and-right-sum-differences/solutions/3232184/clean-js-map-and-reduce/\\\">Array traversal and prefix sums.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    let nums = [1, 2, 3, 4]; // Example input array<br/>\\n    let leftSum = 0; // Initialize leftSum<br/>\\n    let rightSum = nums.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0); // Calculate initial rightSum<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n  //leftSum - (rightSum - curr) <br/>\\n    return nums.map((curr,i)=>{<br/>\\n        rightSum -= curr; // initialized with reduce <br/>\\n        let res = Math.abs(leftSum - rightSum );<br/>\\n        leftSum += curr;<br/>\\n        return res<br/>\\n    });<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize `leftSum` as 0 and `rightSum` as the sum of all elements in `nums`.<br/>2. Iterate through `nums`, updating `leftSum` and `rightSum` for each index.<br/>3. For each index `i`, calculate the absolute difference between `leftSum` and `rightSum` and store it in the result array.<br/>4. Update `leftSum` and `rightSum` accordingly after each iteration.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Description: Explaining the logic of the main solution<br/>\\n    The solution employs a map function to traverse the array, calculating the absolute difference between `leftSum` and `rightSum` at each step, thus efficiently finding the required values without separate sum arrays.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution: Generated based on the problem's requirements<br/>\\n    let result = [];<br/>\\n    for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {<br/>\\n        result.push(Math.abs(leftSum - rightSum));<br/>\\n        rightSum -= nums[i];<br/>\\n        leftSum += nums[i];<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n    return result;<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n), where n is the length of the `nums` array.<br/><br/></div>\"}",
