            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1389. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/create-target-array-in-the-given-order\\\">1389. Create Target Array in the Given Order</a></b></span>\\n<div>Create a target array using two input arrays, `nums` and `index`, by inserting elements from `nums` into the target array at positions specified by `index`.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given two integer arrays: `nums` and `index`.<br/>2. Start with an empty target array.<br/>3. Insert each element from `nums` into the target array at the position specified by the corresponding element in `index`.<br/>4. Perform the insertion process from left to right as per the order in `nums` and `index`.<br/>5. It's guaranteed that the insertion operations are valid.<br/>6. Return the final target array.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>Input: `nums = [0,1,2,3,4], index = [0,1,2,2,1]` => Output: `[0,4,1,3,2]`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [0,1,2,3,4], index = [0,1,2,2,1]<br/>Output: [0,4,1,3,2]<br/>Explanation:<br/>nums       index     target<br/>0            0        [0]<br/>1            1        [0,1]<br/>2            2        [0,1,2]<br/>3            2        [0,1,3,2]<br/>4            1        [0,4,1,3,2]<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,2,3,4,0], index = [0,1,2,3,0]<br/>Output: [0,1,2,3,4]<br/>Explanation:<br/>nums       index     target<br/>1            0        [1]<br/>2            1        [1,2]<br/>3            2        [1,2,3]<br/>4            3        [1,2,3,4]<br/>0            0        [0,1,2,3,4]<br/><br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1], index = [0]<br/>Output: [1]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= nums.length, index.length <= 100<br/>nums.length == index.length<br/>0 <= nums[i] <= 100<br/>0 <= index[i] <= i<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/create-target-array-in-the-given-order/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/create-target-array-in-the-given-order/solutions/548762/fast-simple-javascript-solution/\\\">Array manipulation with insertion.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    let nums = [0,1,2,3,4]; // Example input array of numbers<br/>\\n    let idxArr = [0,1,2,2,1]; // Corresponding array of indices<br/>\\n    let target = []; // Array to store the result<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    const createTargetArray = (nums, idx) => {<br/>\\n        let target = [];<br/>\\n        for (let i = 0; i ＜ nums.length; i++) {<br/>\\n            target.splice(idx[i], 0, nums[i]);<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        return target;<br/>\\n    };<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize an empty array `target` and a variable `max` to track the maximum index encountered.<br/>2. Iterate over `idxArr` and adjust indices to account for previous insertions.<br/>3. For each element in `nums`, insert it into `target` at the index specified in `idxArr`.<br/>4. Return the `target` array.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    The solution uses the `splice` method to insert each element from `nums` into the `target` array at the indices specified in `idxArr`.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    for (let i = 0; i ＜ nums.length; i++) {<br/>\\n        if (idxArr[i] ＜= max) {<br/>\\n            for (let j = 0; j ＜ i; j++) {<br/>\\n                if (idxArr[i] ＜= idxArr[j]) idxArr[j]++;<br/>\\n                if (idxArr[j] > max) max = idxArr[j];<br/>\\n            }<br/>\\n        }<br/>\\n        max = Math.max(max, idxArr[i]);<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n    return idxArr.map((idx, i) => nums[i]); // Construct target array based on adjusted indices<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n^2) due to the nested loops for adjusting indices.<br/><br/></div>\"}",
