            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1313. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/decompress-run-length-encoded-list\\\">1313. Decompress Run-Length Encoded List</a></b></span>\\n<div>Decompress a run-length encoded list to generate a decompressed list.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given a list `nums` representing integers encoded with run-length encoding.<br/>2. Each adjacent pair `[freq, val] = [nums[2*i], nums[2*i+1]]` (for i >= 0) represents `freq` elements with the value `val`.<br/>3. Concatenate sublists generated from each pair to form a decompressed list.<br/>4. Return the decompressed list.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>Input: `nums = [1,2,3,4]` => Output: `[2,4,4,4]`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,2,3,4]<br/>Output: [2,4,4,4]<br/>Explanation: The first pair [1,2] means we have freq = 1 and val = 2 so we generate the array [2].<br/>The second pair [3,4] means we have freq = 3 and val = 4 so we generate [4,4,4].<br/>At the end the concatenation [2] + [4,4,4] is [2,4,4,4].<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [1,1,2,3]<br/>Output: [1,3,3]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>2 <= nums.length <= 100<br/>nums.length % 2 == 0<br/>1 <= nums[i] <= 100<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/decompress-run-length-encoded-list/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/decompress-run-length-encoded-list/solutions/508788/js-simple-javascript-solution/\\\">Run-length decoding using array manipulation.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    let nums = [1, 2, 3, 4]; // Example input array for decompression<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n    const decompressRLElist = nums => <br/>\\n      nums.flatMap((val, i) => i % 2 === 0 ? new Array(nums[i]).fill(nums[i + 1]) : []);<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize an empty array `result`.<br/>2. Loop through `nums`, considering pairs `[nums[i - 1], nums[i]]`.<br/>3. For each pair, create an array of size `nums[i - 1]` filled with `nums[i]`.<br/>4. Concatenate these arrays to form the decompressed list.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    The solution uses `flatMap` to iterate over the input array and for each even-indexed element, it creates and fills a new array with the next element.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    let result = []; // Initialize result array<br/>\\n    for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i += 2) {<br/>\\n        result.push(...new Array(nums[i]).fill(nums[i + 1]));<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n    return result;<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n), where n is the number of elements in the input list.<br/><br/></div>\"}",
