            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1769. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-number-of-operations-to-move-all-balls-to-each-box\\\">1769. Minimum Number of Operations to Move All Balls to Each Box</a></b></span>\\n<div>Calculate the minimum number of operations needed to move all the balls to each box in a given binary string representation of boxes.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You have `n` boxes represented by a binary string `boxes`.<br/>2. `boxes[i]` is '0' if the ith box is empty, and '1' if it contains a ball.<br/>3. You can move a ball to an adjacent box in one operation.<br/>4. Return an array `answer`, where `answer[i]` is the minimum number of operations needed to move all the balls to the ith box.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>`boxes = \\\"110\\\"` => `[1,1,3]`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: boxes = \\\"110\\\"<br/>Output: [1,1,3]<br/>Explanation: The answer for each box is as follows:<br/>1) First box: you will have to move one ball from the second box to the first box in one operation.<br/>2) Second box: you will have to move one ball from the first box to the second box in one operation.<br/>3) Third box: you will have to move one ball from the first box to the third box in two operations, and move one ball from the second box to the third box in one operation.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: boxes = \\\"001011\\\"<br/>Output: [11,8,5,4,3,4]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>n == boxes.length<br/>1 <= n <= 2000<br/>boxes[i] is either '0' or '1'.<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-number-of-operations-to-move-all-balls-to-each-box/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-number-of-operations-to-move-all-balls-to-each-box/solutions/1184205/javascript-easy-to-follow-o-n-92ms/\\\">Use two passes of a linear scan algorithm.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    let boxes = '110'; // Example input string representing boxes<br/>\\n    let result = new Array(boxes.length).fill(0);<br/>\\n    let notEmpty = 0, runningSum = 0;<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n  for (let i = 0; i < boxes.length; ++i) { <br/>\\n    result[i] += runningSum; <br/>\\n    if (boxes[i] === '1') ++notEmpty; <br/>\\n    runningSum += notEmpty; <br/>\\n  } <br/>\\n\\nnotEmpty = 0; <br/>\\n  runningSum = 0;<br/>\\n  \\n  for (let i = boxes.length - 1; i >= 0; --i) {<br/>\\n    result[i] += runningSum;<br/>\\n    if (boxes[i] === '1') ++notEmpty;<br/>\\n    runningSum += notEmpty;<br/>\\n  }<br/>\\n  \\n  return result;<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize an array `result` of the same length as `boxes`, filled with zeros.<br/>2. Make a left-to-right pass:<br/>   - Update `result[i]` with the running sum of operations.<br/>   - Increment a `notEmpty` count for each box containing a ball.<br/>   - Add the `notEmpty` count to `runningSum`.<br/>3. Reset `notEmpty` and `runningSum` to zero.<br/>4. Make a right-to-left pass with similar operations as the first pass.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    The solution calculates the minimum operations for each box by considering the distance and quantity of balls in all other boxes, in both directions.<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>\\n    // Alternative Solution:<br/>\\n    for (let i = 0, leftCount = 0, rightCount = boxes.split('1').length - 1; i ＜ boxes.length; i++) {<br/>\\n        result[i] = leftCount + rightCount;<br/>\\n        if (boxes[i] === '1') { leftCount++; rightCount--; }<br/>\\n    }<br/>\\n    return result;<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n), where n is the length of the `boxes` string.<br/><br/></div>\"}",
