            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1773. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-items-matching-a-rule\\\">1773. Count Items Matching a Rule</a></b></span>\\n<div>Count items in an array matching a specific rule.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You have an array `items`, where each `items[i]` = `[typei, colori, namei]` describes an item's type, color, and name.<br/>2. You're given a rule represented by two strings, `ruleKey` and `ruleValue`.<br/>3. An item matches the rule if:<br/>   - `ruleKey == \\\"type\\\"` and `typei` matches `ruleValue`.<br/>   - `ruleKey == \\\"color\\\"` and `colori` matches `ruleValue`.<br/>   - `ruleKey == \\\"name\\\"` and `namei` matches `ruleValue`.<br/>4. Return the count of items that match the rule.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>`items = [[\\\"phone\\\",\\\"blue\\\",\\\"pixel\\\"],[\\\"computer\\\",\\\"silver\\\",\\\"phone\\\"],[\\\"phone\\\",\\\"gold\\\",\\\"iphone\\\"]], ruleKey = \\\"type\\\", ruleValue = \\\"phone\\\"` => `2`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: items = [[\\\"phone\\\",\\\"blue\\\",\\\"pixel\\\"],[\\\"computer\\\",\\\"silver\\\",\\\"lenovo\\\"],[\\\"phone\\\",\\\"gold\\\",\\\"iphone\\\"]], ruleKey = \\\"color\\\", ruleValue = \\\"silver\\\"<br/>Output: 1<br/>Explanation: There is only one item matching the given rule, which is [\\\"computer\\\",\\\"silver\\\",\\\"lenovo\\\"].<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: items = [[\\\"phone\\\",\\\"blue\\\",\\\"pixel\\\"],[\\\"computer\\\",\\\"silver\\\",\\\"phone\\\"],[\\\"phone\\\",\\\"gold\\\",\\\"iphone\\\"]], ruleKey = \\\"type\\\", ruleValue = \\\"phone\\\"<br/>Output: 2<br/>Explanation: There are only two items matching the given rule, which are [\\\"phone\\\",\\\"blue\\\",\\\"pixel\\\"] and [\\\"phone\\\",\\\"gold\\\",\\\"iphone\\\"]. Note that the item [\\\"computer\\\",\\\"silver\\\",\\\"phone\\\"] does not match.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= items.length <= 104<br/>1 <= typei.length, colori.length, namei.length, ruleValue.length <= 10<br/>ruleKey is equal to either \\\"type\\\", \\\"color\\\", or \\\"name\\\".<br/>All strings consist only of lowercase letters.<br/></div>\\n<span><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-items-matching-a-rule/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-items-matching-a-rule/solutions/1086216/javascript-single-pass-o-n-one-liner-almost/\\\">Array Traversal and Matching (Using `Array.reduce`)</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\">\\n    // Define RULE_IDX to map ruleKey to index in items<br/>\\n    const RULE_IDX = { 'type': 0, 'color': 1, 'name': 2 };<br/>\\n    // Assume items is a 2D array and ruleKey, ruleValue are strings\\n<br/><br/>\\n</div>\\n<div>\\n      items.filter(item => <br/>\\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;item[RULE_IDX[ruleKey]] === ruleValue<br/>\\n      ).length;\\n</div>\\n<div><br/>1. Create a mapping (`RULE_IDX`) to associate `ruleKey` with its index in the item array.<br/>2. Iterate over the `items` array.<br/>3. For each item, check if the element at the index corresponding to `ruleKey` matches `ruleValue`.<br/>4. Count the number of matches.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution iterates over the `items` array and uses the `reduce` method to accumulate the count of items that match the specified rule.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\">\\n    // This alternative solution uses reduce<br/>\\n    items.reduce(<br/>\\n    (ans, item) => <br/>\\n    item[RULE_IDX[ruleKey]] === ruleValue ?  ans + 1 : ans, <br/>\\n      0 );<br/>\\n</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\">O(n), where n is the number of items in the array.</div>\"}",
