            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2798. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-employees-who-met-the-target\\\">2798. Number of Employees Who Met the Target</a></b></span>\\n<div>In this LeetCode problem, we are given an array `hours` representing the number of hours each employee in a company has worked, and a `target` number of hours that each employee is required to work. The task is to return the count of employees who have worked at least the target number of hours.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. **Input Array (`hours`):** An array of non-negative integers, where each element represents the hours worked by an employee. The employees are numbered from 0 to `n-1`.<br/>2. **Target Hours (`target`):** A non-negative integer representing the minimum number of hours each employee needs to work.<br/>3. **Objective:** Determine the number of employees who have worked at least the target number of hours.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [5,1,4,2,2] => 0 (None of the employees met the 6-hour target)</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: hours = [0,1,2,3,4], target = 2<br/>Output: 3<br/>Explanation: The company wants each employee to work for at least 2 hours.<br/>- Employee 0 worked for 0 hours and didn't meet the target.<br/>- Employee 1 worked for 1 hours and didn't meet the target.<br/>- Employee 2 worked for 2 hours and met the target.<br/>- Employee 3 worked for 3 hours and met the target.<br/>- Employee 4 worked for 4 hours and met the target.<br/>There are 3 employees who met the target.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: hours = [5,1,4,2,2], target = 6<br/>Output: 0<br/>Explanation: The company wants each employee to work for at least 6 hours.<br/>There are 0 employees who met the target.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= n == hours.length <= 50<br/>0 <= hours[i], target <= 105<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2AJL4Oh1snk&pp=ygUsMjc5OC4gTnVtYmVyIG9mIEVtcGxveWVlcyBXaG8gTWV0IHRoZSBUYXJnZXQ%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PaduxxgDNZ0&pp=ygU2Mjc5OC4gTnVtYmVyIG9mIEVtcGxveWVlcyBXaG8gTWV0IHRoZSBUYXJnZXRqYXZhc2NyaXB0\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-employees-who-met-the-target/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-employees-who-met-the-target/solutions/4075009/easy-explained/\\\">The solution uses a simple iteration algorithm over the array.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>/**<br/> * @param {number[]} hours<br/> * @param {number} target<br/> * @return {number}<br/> */<br/>var numberOfEmployeesWhoMetTarget = function(hours, target) {<br/>    let count = 0;<br/>};<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>for(let i = 0; i ＜ hours.length; i++) {<br/>        if(hours[i] >= target) count++;<br/>    return count;<br/>};</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize a counter (`count`) to zero.<br/>2. Iterate through each element in the `hours` array.<br/>3. For each element, check if it is greater than or equal to the `target`.<br/>4. If yes, increment the counter (`count`).<br/>5. Return the final value of the counter.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution involves iterating through the `hours` array and comparing each value with the `target`. The counter increments each time an employee's hours are equal to or exceed the target. This approach ensures that all employees' hours are checked against the target, and the count of those meeting or exceeding it is returned.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity of this solution is O(n), where n is the number of elements in the `hours` array. This is because the solution involves a single loop through the array.</div>\"}",
