            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2824. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-pairs-whose-sum-is-less-than-target\\\">2824. Count Pairs Whose Sum is Less than Target</a></b></span>\\n<div>The problem involves finding the number of distinct pairs `(i, j)` in an integer array `nums` such that `nums[i] + nums[j] ＜ target` and `0 ＜= i ＜ j ＜ n`, where `n` is the length of the array.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You are given an integer array `nums` and an integer `target`.<br/>2. You need to find all pairs of indices `(i, j)` in this array, where `0 ＜= i ＜ j ＜ n` (n is the length of `nums`), and the sum of the elements at these indices is strictly less than `target`.<br/>3. Your goal is to return the total count of such pairs.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- `[-1,1,2,3,1]`, `2` => `3`<br/>- `[-6,2,5,-2,-7,-1,3]`, `-2` => `10`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [-1,1,2,3,1], target = 2<br/>Output: 3<br/>Explanation: There are 3 pairs of indices that satisfy the conditions in the statement:<br/>- (0, 1) since 0 < 1 and nums[0] + nums[1] = 0 < target<br/>- (0, 2) since 0 < 2 and nums[0] + nums[2] = 1 < target <br/>- (0, 4) since 0 < 4 and nums[0] + nums[4] = 0 < target<br/>Note that (0, 3) is not counted since nums[0] + nums[3] is not strictly less than the target.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [-6,2,5,-2,-7,-1,3], target = -2<br/>Output: 10<br/>Explanation: There are 10 pairs of indices that satisfy the conditions in the statement:<br/>- (0, 1) since 0 < 1 and nums[0] + nums[1] = -4 < target<br/>- (0, 3) since 0 < 3 and nums[0] + nums[3] = -8 < target<br/>- (0, 4) since 0 < 4 and nums[0] + nums[4] = -13 < target<br/>- (0, 5) since 0 < 5 and nums[0] + nums[5] = -7 < target<br/>- (0, 6) since 0 < 6 and nums[0] + nums[6] = -3 < target<br/>- (1, 4) since 1 < 4 and nums[1] + nums[4] = -5 < target<br/>- (3, 4) since 3 < 4 and nums[3] + nums[4] = -9 < target<br/>- (3, 5) since 3 < 5 and nums[3] + nums[5] = -3 < target<br/>- (4, 5) since 4 < 5 and nums[4] + nums[5] = -8 < target<br/>- (4, 6) since 4 < 6 and nums[4] + nums[6] = -4 < target<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= nums.length == n <= 50<br/>-50 <= nums[i], target <= 50<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uZ8mu6sHmrY&pp=ygUvMjgyNC4gQ291bnQgUGFpcnMgV2hvc2UgU3VtIGlzIExlc3MgdGhhbiBUYXJnZXQ%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xe1teNERwSY&pp=ygU5MjgyNC4gQ291bnQgUGFpcnMgV2hvc2UgU3VtIGlzIExlc3MgdGhhbiBUYXJnZXRqYXZhc2NyaXB0\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-pairs-whose-sum-is-less-than-target/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-pairs-whose-sum-is-less-than-target/solutions/3934290/javascript-easy-solution-with-example/\\\">The solution uses a simple **nested loop** approach to iterate over all possible pairs in the array.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>/**<br/> * @param {number[]} nums<br/> * @param {number} target<br/> * @return {number}<br/> */<br/>var countPairs = function(nums, target) {<br/>    let count = 0; // count initialized to 0<br/>    // ...<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>var countPairs = function(nums, target) {<br/>    nums.sort((a, b) => a - b);<br/>    let count = 0;<br/>    let left = 0, right = nums.length - 1;<br/><br/>    while (left ＜ right) {<br/>        if (nums[left] + nums[right] ＜ target) {<br/>            count += right - left;<br/>            left++;<br/>        } else {<br/>            right--;<br/>        }<br/>    }<br/><br/>    return count;<br/>};</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize a variable `count` to zero. This will keep track of the number of valid pairs found.<br/>2. Use a nested loop: the outer loop iterates over each element in the array using index `i`, and the inner loop iterates over the elements following the `i`th element using index `j`.<br/>3. Inside the inner loop, check if the sum of elements at indices `i` and `j` (`nums[i] + nums[j]`) is less than the target.<br/>4. If the condition is met, increment `count`.<br/>5. After all iterations, return the value of `count`.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>- An alternative solution is to first sort the array and then use a two-pointer technique to find pairs.<br/>- This approach can potentially be more efficient than the nested loop, especially for larger arrays, as it reduces the number of unnecessary comparisons.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>var countPairs = function(nums, target) {<br/>    let count = 0;<br/><br/>    for (let i = 0; i ＜ nums.length; i++) {<br/>        for (let j = i + 1; j ＜ nums.length; j++) {<br/>            if (nums[i] + nums[j] ＜ target) {<br/>                count++;<br/>            }<br/>        }<br/>    }<br/><br/>    return count;<br/>};</br></br>The provided solution iterates over all possible pairs in the array and checks if their sum is less than the target. It's straightforward and easy to understand but can be inefficient for larger arrays due to its nested loop structure.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity of this solution is **O(n²)**, where `n` is the length of the array. This is because there are two nested loops, each iterating up to `n` times.<br/><br/>---</div>\"}",
