            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1365. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/how-many-numbers-are-smaller-than-the-current-number\\\">1365. How Many Numbers Are Smaller Than the Current Number</a></b></span>\\n<div>The problem requires finding, for each element in an array `nums`, how many elements are smaller than it and returning the counts in a new array.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You are given an integer array `nums`.<br/>2. For each element `nums[i]`, count how many elements in `nums` are smaller than `nums[i]`.<br/>3. Return an array where the `i`th element is the count of elements smaller than `nums[i]`.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- `[8,1,2,2,3]` => `[4,0,1,1,3]`<br/>- `[6,5,4,8]` => `[2,1,0,3]`<br/>- `[7,7,7,7]` => `[0,0,0,0]`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [8,1,2,2,3]<br/>Output: [4,0,1,1,3]<br/>Explanation: <br/>For nums[0]=8 there exist four smaller numbers than it (1, 2, 2 and 3). <br/>For nums[1]=1 does not exist any smaller number than it.<br/>For nums[2]=2 there exist one smaller number than it (1). <br/>For nums[3]=2 there exist one smaller number than it (1). <br/>For nums[4]=3 there exist three smaller numbers than it (1, 2 and 2).<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [6,5,4,8]<br/>Output: [2,1,0,3]<br/><br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [7,7,7,7]<br/>Output: [0,0,0,0]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>2 <= nums.length <= 500<br/>0 <= nums[i] <= 100<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MjpNK4x2U0k&pp=ygU6MTM2NS4gSG93IE1hbnkgTnVtYmVycyBBcmUgU21hbGxlciBUaGFuIHRoZSBDdXJyZW50IE51bWJlcg%3D%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MjpNK4x2U0k&pp=ygVEMTM2NS4gSG93IE1hbnkgTnVtYmVycyBBcmUgU21hbGxlciBUaGFuIHRoZSBDdXJyZW50IE51bWJlcmphdmFzY3JpcHQ%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/how-many-numbers-are-smaller-than-the-current-number/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/how-many-numbers-are-smaller-than-the-current-number/solutions/547953/faster-than-98-32-memory-usage-less-than-100-00-2-lines-of-code/\\\">The solution uses **sorting** and the **map** function.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>var smallerNumbersThanCurrent = function(nums) {<br/>    const sorted = [...nums].sort((a, b) => a - b); // Copy and sort nums<br/>    // ...<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>var smallerNumbersThanCurrent = function(nums) {<br/>    const sorted = [...nums].sort((a, b) => a - b);<br/>    return nums.map(num => sorted.indexOf(num));</div>\\n<div>1. Make a copy of the `nums` array and sort it in ascending order. This sorted array will help in determining the rank of each element.<br/>2. Use the `map` function to transform each element in the original `nums` array.<br/>3. For each element in `nums`, find its first occurrence in the sorted array using `indexOf`. This gives the number of elements smaller than the current element.<br/>4. Return the array formed by these counts.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution involves sorting a copy of the original array and then using the position of each element in the sorted array to determine how many numbers are smaller than it. The use of `indexOf` on the sorted array ensures that the count reflects the number of smaller elements.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>var smallerNumbersThanCurrent = function(nums) {<br/>    const counts = new Array(101).fill(0);<br/>    nums.forEach(num => counts[num]++);<br/><br/>    for (let i = 1; i ＜ 101; i++) {<br/>        counts[i] += counts[i - 1];<br/>    }<br/><br/>    return nums.map(num => num == 0 ? 0 : counts[num - 1]);<br/>};</br></br><br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity of this solution is **O(n log n)** due to sorting, where `n` is the length of the array. The `map` and `indexOf` operations contribute additional complexity, but the dominant factor is the sorting.<br/><br/>---</div>\"}",
