            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2161. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/partition-array-according-to-given-pivot\\\">2161. Partition Array According to Given Pivot</a></b></span>\\n<div>The problem requires rearranging an array `nums` around a given `pivot` value such that all elements less than the pivot are before it, all elements equal to it are next, and all elements greater than it are after, maintaining their relative order.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You are given an integer array `nums` and an integer `pivot`.<br/>2. Rearrange `nums` so that:<br/>   - All elements less than `pivot` appear before elements equal to or greater than `pivot`.<br/>   - All elements equal to `pivot` appear after elements less than and before elements greater than `pivot`.<br/>   - The relative order of elements less than and greater than `pivot` is maintained.<br/>3. Return the rearranged array.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- `[9,12,5,10,14,3,10]`, `10` => `[9,5,3,10,10,12,14]`<br/>- `[-3,4,3,2]`, `2` => `[-3,2,4,3]`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [9,12,5,10,14,3,10], pivot = 10<br/>Output: [9,5,3,10,10,12,14]<br/>Explanation: <br/>The elements 9, 5, and 3 are less than the pivot so they are on the left side of the array.<br/>The elements 12 and 14 are greater than the pivot so they are on the right side of the array.<br/>The relative ordering of the elements less than and greater than pivot is also maintained. [9, 5, 3] and [12, 14] are the respective orderings.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [-3,4,3,2], pivot = 2<br/>Output: [-3,2,4,3]<br/>Explanation: <br/>The element -3 is less than the pivot so it is on the left side of the array.<br/>The elements 4 and 3 are greater than the pivot so they are on the right side of the array.<br/>The relative ordering of the elements less than and greater than pivot is also maintained. [-3] and [4, 3] are the respective orderings.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= nums.length <= 105<br/>-106 <= nums[i] <= 106<br/>pivot equals to an element of nums.<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ie7eN2NAa6w&pp=ygUuMjE2MS4gUGFydGl0aW9uIEFycmF5IEFjY29yZGluZyB0byBHaXZlbiBQaXZvdA%3D%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/JSVjc-01oG8\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/partition-array-according-to-given-pivot/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/partition-array-according-to-given-pivot/solutions/2480491/simple-js-solution-w-comments-two-pointers/\\\">The solution uses a **two-pointer approach** with additional space for the output array.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>const pivotArray = (nums, pivot) => {<br/>    let N = nums.length;<br/>    let output = new Array(N); // Initialize output array<br/><br/>    let i = 0; // Start pointer<br/>    let j = N - 1; // End pointer<br/><br/>    let L = 0; // Left fill pointer<br/>    let R = N - 1; // Right fill pointer<br/>    <br/>    // ...<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>const pivotArray = (nums, pivot) => {<br/>    let N = nums.length;<br/>    let output = [];<br/><br/>    let i = 0;<br/>    let j = N - 1;<br/><br/>    let L = 0;<br/>    let R = N - 1;<br/>    <br/>    while (i ＜ nums.length) {<br/>        if (nums[i] ＜ pivot) output[L++] = nums[i];<br/>        if (nums[j] > pivot) output[R--] = nums[j];<br/><br/>        i++;<br/>        j--;<br/>    }<br/><br/>    while (L ＜= R) {<br/>        output[L++] = pivot;<br/><br/>    return output;<br/>};</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize an array `output` of the same length as `nums`.<br/>2. Use two pointers, `i` starting from the beginning and `j` starting from the end of `nums`.<br/>3. Use two more pointers, `L` and `R`, to fill the `output` array from the left and right, respectively.<br/>4. Iterate over `nums` using `i` and `j`. If `nums[i]` is less than the pivot, place it at the current `L` position in `output` and increment `L`. If `nums[j]` is greater than the pivot, place it at the current `R` position in `output` and decrement `R`.<br/>5. Once all elements less than and greater than the pivot are placed, fill the middle of `output` with the pivot value.<br/>6. Return the `output` array.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>This solution effectively partitions the array into three sections (less than, equal to, and greater than the pivot) while preserving the relative order of elements. It utilizes additional space for the output array and two pointers for efficient traversal.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>const pivotArray = (nums, pivot) => {<br/>    let less = [];<br/>    let equal = [];<br/>    let greater = [];<br/><br/>    for (let num of nums) {<br/>        if (num ＜ pivot) less.push(num);<br/>        else if (num > pivot) greater.push(num);<br/>        else equal.push(num);<br/>    }<br/><br/>    return less.concat(equal, greater);<br/>};</br></br><br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity of this solution is **O(N)**, where `N` is the length of the array. This efficiency is achieved because each element of the array is processed only once.<br/><br/>---</div>\"}",
