            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1528. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/shuffle-string\\\">1528. Shuffle String</a></b></span>\\n<div>The problem involves shuffling a string `s` based on an integer array `indices`. Each character in the string `s` is moved to a new position as indicated by the corresponding value in `indices`, and the goal is to return the shuffled string.<img src=\\\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/07/09/q1.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" class=\\\"resize-img\\\"></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You are given a string `s` and an integer array `indices` of the same length.<br/>2. The string `s` needs to be rearranged such that each character at the `i`th position is moved to the position `indices[i]`.<br/>3. The task is to return the shuffled string after this rearrangement.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- `s = \\\"codeleet\\\"`, `indices = [4,5,6,7,0,2,1,3]` => `\\\"leetcode\\\"`<br/>- `s = \\\"abc\\\"`, `indices = [0,1,2]` => `\\\"abc\\\"`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: s = \\\"codeleet\\\", indices = [4,5,6,7,0,2,1,3]<br/>Output: \\\"leetcode\\\"<br/>Explanation: As shown, \\\"codeleet\\\" becomes \\\"leetcode\\\" after shuffling.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: s = \\\"abc\\\", indices = [0,1,2]<br/>Output: \\\"abc\\\"<br/>Explanation: After shuffling, each character remains in its position.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>s.length == indices.length == n<br/>1 <= n <= 100<br/>s consists of only lowercase English letters.<br/>0 <= indices[i] < n<br/>All values of indices are unique.<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DWXSrhlvE00&pp=ygUUMTUyOC4gU2h1ZmZsZSBTdHJpbmc%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dkDCzw8YxVI&pp=ygUeMTUyOC4gU2h1ZmZsZSBTdHJpbmdqYXZhc2NyaXB0\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/shuffle-string/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/shuffle-string/solutions/813928/my-javascript-solution-99/\\\">The solution uses an <b>array</b> for repositioning characters based on `indices`.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>var restoreString = function(s, indices) {<br/>    var len = indices.length;<br/>    var str = new Array(len); // Initialize array of length len<br/><br/>    // Loop through the string s<br/>    for(let i = 0; i ＜ len; i++){<br/>        // ...<br/>    // ...<br/>};<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>var restoreString = function(s, indices) {<br/>    var len = indices.length;<br/>    var str = new Array(len);<br/>    for(let i = 0; i ＜ len; i++){<br/>        str[indices[i]] = s[i];<br/>    return str.join(\\\"\\\");  <br/>};</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize an array `str` of the same length as `indices`.<br/>2. Loop through each character of `s`.<br/>3. For each index `i`, place the character `s[i]` at the position `indices[i]` in the array `str`.<br/>4. After filling the array `str`, join its elements to form the shuffled string.<br/>5. Return the shuffled string.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>This solution effectively reconstructs the string by positioning each character at its designated index as specified by `indices`. It uses a separate array to hold the characters in their new positions before joining them to form the final string.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>var restoreString = function(s, indices) {<br/>    return indices.map((val, index) => s[indices.indexOf(index)]).join('');<br/>};</br></br><br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity of this solution is <b>O(n)</b>, where `n` is the length of the string `s`. Each character is processed exactly once.<br/><br/>---</div>\"}",
