            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1816. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/truncate-sentence\\\">1816. Truncate Sentence</a></b></span>\\n<div>The problem is to truncate a given sentence `s` such that it contains only the first `k` words. The sentence has no leading or trailing spaces and words are separated by a single space.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. A sentence `s` is given, consisting of uppercase and lowercase English letters, separated by single spaces.<br/>2. An integer `k` is provided, which represents the number of words to keep from the start of the sentence.<br/>3. The task is to return the sentence after keeping only the first `k` words.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- `s = \\\"Hello how are you Contestant\\\"`, `k = 4` => `\\\"Hello how are you\\\"`<br/>- `s = \\\"What is the solution to this problem\\\"`, `k = 4` => `\\\"What is the solution\\\"`<br/>- `s = \\\"chopper is not a tanuki\\\"`, `k = 5` => `\\\"chopper is not a tanuki\\\"`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: s = \\\"Hello how are you Contestant\\\", k = 4<br/>Output: \\\"Hello how are you\\\"<br/>Explanation:<br/>The words in s are [\\\"Hello\\\", \\\"how\\\" \\\"are\\\", \\\"you\\\", \\\"Contestant\\\"].<br/>The first 4 words are [\\\"Hello\\\", \\\"how\\\", \\\"are\\\", \\\"you\\\"].<br/>Hence, you should return \\\"Hello how are you\\\".<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: s = \\\"What is the solution to this problem\\\", k = 4<br/>Output: \\\"What is the solution\\\"<br/>Explanation:<br/>The words in s are [\\\"What\\\", \\\"is\\\" \\\"the\\\", \\\"solution\\\", \\\"to\\\", \\\"this\\\", \\\"problem\\\"].<br/>The first 4 words are [\\\"What\\\", \\\"is\\\", \\\"the\\\", \\\"solution\\\"].<br/>Hence, you should return \\\"What is the solution\\\".<br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: s = \\\"chopper is not a tanuki\\\", k = 5<br/>Output: \\\"chopper is not a tanuki\\\"<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= s.length <= 500<br/>k is in the range [1, the number of words in s].<br/>s consist of only lowercase and uppercase English letters and spaces.<br/>The words in s are separated by a single space.<br/>There are no leading or trailing spaces.<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kWmzOIp1Ed4&pp=ygUXMTgxNi4gVHJ1bmNhdGUgU2VudGVuY2U%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_odcYEt2Ps8&pp=ygUhMTgxNi4gVHJ1bmNhdGUgU2VudGVuY2VqYXZhc2NyaXB0\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/truncate-sentence/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/truncate-sentence/solutions/1143981/javascript-easy-to-understand-2-solutions/\\\">The solution uses <b>string manipulation</b> methods like `split` and `join`.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>const truncateSentence = (s, k) => {<br/>    // Split the sentence into words, limit to k words<br/>    // ...<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>const truncateSentence = (s, k) => {<br/>  let spaceCount = 0;<br/>  for (let i = 0; i ＜ s.length; ++i) {<br/>    if (s[i] === ' ' && ++spaceCount === k) return s.slice(0, i);<br/>  }<br/>  return s;<br/>};</div>\\n<div>1. Split the sentence `s` into an array of words using `split(' ', k)`, limiting the split to `k` words.<br/>2. Join the first `k` words back into a string using `join(' ')`.<br/>3. Return the resulting string.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/><br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>const truncateSentence = (s, k) => s.split(' ', k).join(' ');</br></br>The solution effectively truncates the sentence by splitting it into words, taking the first `k` words, and joining them back into a sentence. This approach is straightforward and leverages built-in string manipulation functions in JavaScript.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity of this solution is <b>O(n)</b>, where `n` is the length of the sentence. The split operation is the dominant factor in the time complexity.<br/><br/>---</div>\"}",
