            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1630. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/arithmetic-subarrays\\\">1630. Arithmetic Subarrays</a></b></span>\\n<div>The task is to determine if subarrays of a given array can be rearranged into arithmetic sequences, based on specified queries.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given an array `nums` of integers and two arrays `l` and `r` representing range queries.<br/>2. For each query `[l[i], r[i]]`, check if the subarray `nums[l[i]], nums[l[i]+1], ... , nums[r[i]]` can form an arithmetic sequence when rearranged.<br/>3. Return a list of boolean values corresponding to each query.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- `nums = [4,6,5,9,3,7]`, `l = [0,0,2]`, `r = [2,3,5]` => `[true, false, true]`<br/>- `nums = [-12,-9,-3,-12,-6,15,20,-25,-20,-15,-10]`, `l = [0,1,6,4,8,7]`, `r = [4,4,9,7,9,10]` => `[false, true, false, false, true, true]`</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [4,6,5,9,3,7], l = [0,0,2], r = [2,3,5]<br/>Output: [true,false,true]<br/>Explanation:<br/>In the 0th query, the subarray is [4,6,5]. This can be rearranged as [6,5,4], which is an arithmetic sequence.<br/>In the 1st query, the subarray is [4,6,5,9]. This cannot be rearranged as an arithmetic sequence.<br/>In the 2nd query, the subarray is [5,9,3,7]. This can be rearranged as [3,5,7,9], which is an arithmetic sequence.<br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [-12,-9,-3,-12,-6,15,20,-25,-20,-15,-10], l = [0,1,6,4,8,7], r = [4,4,9,7,9,10]<br/>Output: [false,true,false,false,true,true]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>n == nums.length<br/>m == l.length<br/>m == r.length<br/>2 <= n <= 500<br/>1 <= m <= 500<br/>0 <= l[i] < r[i] < n<br/>-105 <= nums[i] <= 105<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zul5uok4IpQ&pp=ygUaMTYzMC4gQXJpdGhtZXRpYyBTdWJhcnJheXM%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MGtpO0hP8VM&pp=ygUkMTYzMC4gQXJpdGhtZXRpYyBTdWJhcnJheXNqYXZhc2NyaXB0\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/arithmetic-subarrays/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/arithmetic-subarrays/solutions/914185/1630-javascript-1-line-solution/\\\">The solution involves <b>sorting subarrays</b> and checking for arithmetic progression.</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>const checkArithmeticSubarrays = (nums, l, r) => {<br/>  // Map over the range queries<br/>  return l.map((start, mapIdx) => {<br/>    // Sort the subarray for each query<br/>    let sortedSubarray = nums.slice(start, r[mapIdx] + 1).sort((a, b) => a - b);<br/>    // ...<br/>  });<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>const checkArithmeticSubarraysAlt = (nums, l, r) => {<br/>  const isArithmetic = (arr) => {<br/>    const diff = arr[1] - arr[0];<br/>    for (let i = 2; i ＜ arr.length; i++) {<br/>      if (arr[i] - arr[i - 1] !== diff) {<br/>        return false;<br/>      }<br/>    }<br/>    return true;<br/>  };<br/><br/>  return l.map((start, i) => {<br/>    const subarray = nums.slice(start, r[i] + 1).sort((a, b) => a - b);<br/>    return isArithmetic(subarray);<br/>  });<br/>};<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>1. Iterate over each query range using `map`, extracting the start and end indices from `l` and `r`.<br/>2. For each query, create a sorted subarray of `nums` from `start` to `end`.<br/>3. Check if the sorted subarray forms an arithmetic sequence using `every`. The difference between consecutive elements should be constant.<br/>4. Return an array of boolean values indicating whether each subarray can form an arithmetic sequence.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/><br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>const checkArithmeticSubarrays = (nums, l, r) =><br/>  l.map((start, mapIdx) =><br/>    nums<br/>      .slice(start, r[mapIdx] + 1)<br/>      .sort((a, b) => a - b)<br/>      .every((n, everyIdx, arr, diff = arr[1] - arr[0]) =><br/>        everyIdx ＜ 2 ? true : n - arr[everyIdx - 1] === diff,<br/>      ),<br/>  );</br></br>The solution methodically checks each subarray, first by sorting it and then ensuring that the difference between consecutive elements remains constant, which is the definition of an arithmetic sequence.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity of this solution is <b>O(m * n log n)</b>, where `m` is the number of queries and `n` is the size of the subarray. Sorting each subarray is the most time-consuming part.<br/><br/>---</div>\"}",
