            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1630. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/arithmetic-subarrays\\\">1630. Arithmetic Subarrays</a></b></span>\\n<div>Determine if subarrays of a given array can be rearranged into arithmetic sequences based on specified range queries.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. You are given three arrays: `nums`, `l`, and `r`.<br/>2. `nums` is an array of integers.<br/>3. `l` and `r` are arrays representing range queries, where the ith query corresponds to the range `[l[i], r[i]]` in `nums`.<br/>4. A subarray of `nums` within a given range is considered valid if it can be rearranged into an arithmetic sequence.<br/>5. An arithmetic sequence is one where the difference between consecutive elements is constant.<br/>6. The task is to return a list of boolean values indicating whether each subarray specified by the range queries can form an arithmetic sequence.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- <b>Example 1</b>: [nums = [4,6,5,9,3,7], l = [0,0,2], r = [2,3,5]] => [true,false,true]</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [4,6,5,9,3,7], l = [0,0,2], r = [2,3,5]<br/>Output: [true,false,true]<br/>Explanation:<br/>In the 0th query, the subarray is [4,6,5]. This can be rearranged as [6,5,4], which is an arithmetic sequence.<br/>In the 1st query, the subarray is [4,6,5,9]. This cannot be rearranged as an arithmetic sequence.<br/>In the 2nd query, the subarray is [5,9,3,7]. This can be rearranged as [3,5,7,9], which is an arithmetic sequence.<br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [-12,-9,-3,-12,-6,15,20,-25,-20,-15,-10], l = [0,1,6,4,8,7], r = [4,4,9,7,9,10]<br/>Output: [false,true,false,false,true,true]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>n == nums.length<br/>m == l.length<br/>m == r.length<br/>2 <= n <= 500<br/>1 <= m <= 500<br/>0 <= l[i] < r[i] < n<br/>-105 <= nums[i] <= 105<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zul5uok4IpQ&pp=ygUaMTYzMC4gQXJpdGhtZXRpYyBTdWJhcnJheXM%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MGtpO0hP8VM&pp=ygUkMTYzMC4gQXJpdGhtZXRpYyBTdWJhcnJheXNqYXZhc2NyaXB0\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/arithmetic-subarrays/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/arithmetic-subarrays/solutions/914185/1630-javascript-1-line-solution/\\\">- Algorithm: Sorting and Checking Arithmetic Progression</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>const checkArithmeticSubarrays = (nums, l, r) => {<br/>  // nums: original array<br/>  // l, r: arrays representing the range queries<br/>  return l.map((start, mapIdx) => {<br/>    // mapIdx: index in the l and r arrays<br/>    // Extract subarray from nums based on the current range query<br/>    // Sort the subarray<br/>    // Check if sorted subarray forms an arithmetic sequence<br/>  });<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>const checkArithmeticSubarrays = (nums, l, r) =><br/>  l.map((start, mapIdx) =><br/>    nums<br/>      .slice(start, r[mapIdx] + 1)<br/>      .sort((a, b) => a - b)<br/>      .every((n, everyIdx, arr, diff = arr[1] - arr[0]) =><br/>        everyIdx ＜ 2 ? true : n - arr[everyIdx - 1] === diff,<br/>      ),<br/>  );</div>\\n<div>1. Iterate over the range queries using `map`, accessing the start index from `l` and the corresponding end index from `r`.<br/>2. For each query, extract the relevant subarray from `nums` using `slice(start, r[mapIdx] + 1)`.<br/>3. Sort the extracted subarray in ascending order.<br/>4. Use `every` to check if the sorted subarray forms an arithmetic sequence. This is done by ensuring that the difference between each pair of consecutive elements is the same.<br/>5. The difference is calculated only once (for the first two elements) and used as a reference for subsequent comparisons.<br/>6. Return a boolean value for each subarray indicating whether it forms an arithmetic sequence.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution involves iterating through each range query, extracting and sorting the relevant subarray, and then checking if the sorted subarray is an arithmetic sequence. The efficiency of the solution depends heavily on the sorting algorithm used (typically O(n log n)) and the linear scan to check for the arithmetic progression.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity of the solution is O(m * n log n), where m is the number of queries and n is the size of the subarray in the worst case. This is due to the sorting operation within each query.</div>\"}",
