            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1409. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/queries-on-a-permutation-with-key\\\">1409. Queries on a Permutation With Key</a></b></span>\\n<div>Process a sequence of queries by finding the position of each query element in a permutation and then moving that element to the beginning of the permutation, returning the positions for each query.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. A permutation `P` of numbers from 1 to `m` is given.<br/>2. An array of queries `queries` is processed sequentially.<br/>3. For each element in `queries`, find its position in `P`.<br/>4. After finding the position, move the element to the beginning of `P`.<br/>5. Record the found positions for each query in an array and return this array.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [queries = [3,1,2,1], m = 5] => [2,1,2,1]</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: queries = [3,1,2,1], m = 5<br/>Output: [2,1,2,1] <br/>Explanation: The queries are processed as follow: <br/>For i=0: queries[i]=3, P=[1,2,3,4,5], position of 3 in P is 2, then we move 3 to the beginning of P resulting in P=[3,1,2,4,5]. <br/>For i=1: queries[i]=1, P=[3,1,2,4,5], position of 1 in P is 1, then we move 1 to the beginning of P resulting in P=[1,3,2,4,5]. <br/>For i=2: queries[i]=2, P=[1,3,2,4,5], position of 2 in P is 2, then we move 2 to the beginning of P resulting in P=[2,1,3,4,5]. <br/>For i=3: queries[i]=1, P=[2,1,3,4,5], position of 1 in P is 1, then we move 1 to the beginning of P resulting in P=[1,2,3,4,5]. <br/>Therefore, the array containing the result is [2,1,2,1].  <br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: queries = [4,1,2,2], m = 4<br/>Output: [3,1,2,0]<br/><br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: queries = [7,5,5,8,3], m = 8<br/>Output: [6,5,0,7,5]<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= m <= 10^3<br/>1 <= queries.length <= m<br/>1 <= queries[i] <= m<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vtkt0Gu3CNY&pp=ygUnMTQwOS4gUXVlcmllcyBvbiBhIFBlcm11dGF0aW9uIFdpdGggS2V5\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dhhDtRPRFzA&pp=ygUxMTQwOS4gUXVlcmllcyBvbiBhIFBlcm11dGF0aW9uIFdpdGggS2V5amF2YXNjcmlwdA%3D%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/queries-on-a-permutation-with-key/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/queries-on-a-permutation-with-key/solutions/2009611/javascript-easy-solution/\\\">- Algorithm: Sequential Processing with Array Manipulation</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>```javascript<br/>function processQueries(queries, m) {<br/>    let result = []; // To store the positions found<br/>    let arr = [];    // Initial permutation P<br/>    for(let i = 1; i ＜= m; i++){<br/>        arr.push(i); // Create the initial permutation P<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>```javascript<br/>function processQueries(queries, m) {<br/>    let result = [];<br/>    let arr = [];<br/>    for(let i = 1; i ＜= m; i++){<br/>        arr.push(i);</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize an array `arr` to represent the permutation `P`, populating it with numbers from 1 to `m`.<br/>2. Initialize an array `result` to store the positions of each query element.<br/>3. Iterate over each element in `queries`.<br/>4. For each query, find the index of the query element in `arr`.<br/>5. Push this index to `result`.<br/>6. Modify `arr` by moving the query element to the beginning.<br/>7. Continue until all queries are processed.<br/>8. Return `result`.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution involves sequentially processing each query, finding the position of the query element in the current permutation, and updating the permutation by moving the query element to the front. This method uses basic array operations like `indexOf` for finding positions and `splice` combined with `concat` for array manipulation.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity of the solution is O(n*m), where n is the length of the queries array and m is the size of the permutation. This is due to the `indexOf` operation being O(m) for each of the n queries.</div>\"}",
