            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2367. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-arithmetic-triplets\\\">2367. Number of Arithmetic Triplets</a></b></span>\\n<div>Count the number of unique arithmetic triplets in a strictly increasing integer array based on a given difference.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. `nums`: A strictly increasing integer array.<br/>2. `diff`: A positive integer representing the required difference for an arithmetic triplet.<br/>3. A triplet (i, j, k) is considered an arithmetic triplet if:<br/>   - i ＜ j ＜ k,<br/>   - nums[j] - nums[i] == diff, and<br/>   - nums[k] - nums[j] == diff.<br/>4. The task is to return the count of unique arithmetic triplets in `nums`.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [nums = [0,1,4,6,7,10], diff = 3] => 2</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [0,1,4,6,7,10], diff = 3<br/>Output: 2<br/>Explanation:<br/>(1, 2, 4) is an arithmetic triplet because both 7 - 4 == 3 and 4 - 1 == 3.<br/>(2, 4, 5) is an arithmetic triplet because both 10 - 7 == 3 and 7 - 4 == 3. <br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [4,5,6,7,8,9], diff = 2<br/>Output: 2<br/>Explanation:<br/>(0, 2, 4) is an arithmetic triplet because both 8 - 6 == 2 and 6 - 4 == 2.<br/>(1, 3, 5) is an arithmetic triplet because both 9 - 7 == 2 and 7 - 5 == 2.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>3 <= nums.length <= 200<br/>0 <= nums[i] <= 200<br/>1 <= diff <= 50<br/>nums is strictly increasing.<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4177N84zOaU&pp=ygUjMjM2Ny4gTnVtYmVyIG9mIEFyaXRobWV0aWMgVHJpcGxldHM%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f6i__1fl2_M&pp=ygUtMjM2Ny4gTnVtYmVyIG9mIEFyaXRobWV0aWMgVHJpcGxldHNqYXZhc2NyaXB0\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-arithmetic-triplets/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-arithmetic-triplets/solutions/2441623/easy-hashmap-solution-and-got-54ms/\\\">- Algorithm: Hash Map</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>```javascript<br/>var arithmeticTriplets = function(nums, diff) {<br/>    let hash = new Map(); // Hash map to store elements of nums<br/>    let count = 0;        // Counter for arithmetic triplets<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>```javascript<br/>var arithmeticTriplets = function(nums, diff) {<br/>    let hash = new Map();<br/>    let count = 0;</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize a hash map `hash` and a counter `count`.<br/>2. Iterate through `nums`.<br/>3. For each element in `nums`, calculate `temp` as the current element minus `diff`.<br/>4. Check if `hash` contains both `temp` and `temp - diff`.<br/>5. If both are present, increment `count`.<br/>6. Add the current element to `hash`.<br/>7. Continue until all elements are processed.<br/>8. Return `count`.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution uses a hash map to keep track of the elements encountered in `nums`. For each element, it checks if the elements forming a potential arithmetic triplet are present in the hash map. If so, it increments the count of triplets. This approach efficiently checks for the presence of required elements to form an arithmetic triplet.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity of the solution is O(n), where n is the number of elements in `nums`. This is due to the single pass through the array.</div>\"}",
