            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 2828. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/check-if-a-string-is-an-acronym-of-words\\\">2828. Check if a String Is an Acronym of Words</a></b></span>\\n<div>Generate a matrix representing the largest value in each contiguous 3x3 submatrix of a given matrix.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given an `n x n` integer matrix `grid`.<br/>2. Create a new matrix `maxLocal` of size `(n - 2) x (n - 2)`.<br/>3. Each element of `maxLocal[i][j]` is the maximum value of the 3x3 submatrix in `grid`, centered around `grid[i + 1][j + 1]`.<br/>4. Return `maxLocal`.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [grid = [[9,9,8,1],[5,6,2,6],[8,2,6,4],[6,2,2,2]]] => [[9,9],[8,6]]</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: words = [\\\"alice\\\",\\\"bob\\\",\\\"charlie\\\"], s = \\\"abc\\\"<br/>Output: true<br/>Explanation: The first character in the words \\\"alice\\\", \\\"bob\\\", and \\\"charlie\\\" are 'a', 'b', and 'c', respectively. Hence, s = \\\"abc\\\" is the acronym. <br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: words = [\\\"an\\\",\\\"apple\\\"], s = \\\"a\\\"<br/>Output: false<br/>Explanation: The first character in the words \\\"an\\\" and \\\"apple\\\" are 'a' and 'a', respectively. <br/>The acronym formed by concatenating these characters is \\\"aa\\\". <br/>Hence, s = \\\"a\\\" is not the acronym.<br/><br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: words = [\\\"never\\\",\\\"gonna\\\",\\\"give\\\",\\\"up\\\",\\\"on\\\",\\\"you\\\"], s = \\\"ngguoy\\\"<br/>Output: true<br/>Explanation: By concatenating the first character of the words in the array, we get the string \\\"ngguoy\\\". <br/>Hence, s = \\\"ngguoy\\\" is the acronym.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= words.length <= 100<br/>1 <= words[i].length <= 10<br/>1 <= s.length <= 100<br/>words[i] and s consist of lowercase English letters.<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GcgV-AtAmkg&pp=ygUuMjgyOC4gQ2hlY2sgaWYgYSBTdHJpbmcgSXMgYW4gQWNyb255bSBvZiBXb3Jkcw%3D%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GcgV-AtAmkg&pp=ygU4MjgyOC4gQ2hlY2sgaWYgYSBTdHJpbmcgSXMgYW4gQWNyb255bSBvZiBXb3Jkc2phdmFzY3JpcHQ%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/check-if-a-string-is-an-acronym-of-words/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/check-if-a-string-is-an-acronym-of-words/solutions/3972516/one-line-solution-javascript-easy/\\\">- Algorithm: Iterative Submatrix Max Calculation</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>```javascript<br/>var largestLocal = function(grid) {<br/>    const matrix = new Array(grid.length - 2).fill(0)<br/>                    .map(() => new Array(grid[0].length - 2).fill(0));<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>```javascript<br/>var largestLocal = function(grid) {<br/>    const matrix = new Array(grid.length - 2).fill(0)<br/>                    .map(() => new Array(grid[0].length - 2).fill(0));</div>\\n<div>1. Create a new matrix `matrix` of size `(n - 2) x (n - 2)`.<br/>2. Iterate over `grid`, excluding the last two rows and columns.<br/>3. For each position `(i, j)`, find the maximum value in the 3x3 submatrix centered at `(i + 1, j + 1)`.<br/>4. Assign this maximum value to `matrix[i][j]`.<br/>5. Return `matrix` after completing the iterations.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution involves iterating through each possible 3x3 submatrix in the original grid and calculating the maximum value in each submatrix. These maximum values are stored in a new matrix, representing the largest values from each submatrix.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n^2), where n is the dimension of the grid. This is due to iterating over almost the entire grid for each element in the new matrix.</div>\"}",
