            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1572. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/matrix-diagonal-sum\\\">1572. Matrix Diagonal Sum</a></b></span>\\n<div>Calculate the sum of the elements on the primary and secondary diagonals of a square matrix, excluding any overlapping elements.<img src=\\\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/08/14/sample_1911.png\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" class=\\\"resize-img\\\"></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given a square matrix `mat`.<br/>2. Compute the sum of all elements on both the primary diagonal (from top-left to bottom-right) and the secondary diagonal (from top-right to bottom-left).<br/>3. Exclude any elements that are part of both diagonals.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [mat = [[1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,9]]] => 25</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: mat = [[1,2,3],<br/>              [4,5,6],<br/>              [7,8,9]]<br/>Output: 25<br/>Explanation: Diagonals sum: 1 + 5 + 9 + 3 + 7 = 25<br/>Notice that element mat[1][1] = 5 is counted only once.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: mat = [[1,1,1,1],<br/>              [1,1,1,1],<br/>              [1,1,1,1],<br/>              [1,1,1,1]]<br/>Output: 8<br/><br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: mat = [[5]]<br/>Output: 5<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>n == mat.length == mat[i].length<br/>1 <= n <= 100<br/>1 <= mat[i][j] <= 100<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VyG8G5nwG7Q&pp=ygUZMTU3Mi4gTWF0cml4IERpYWdvbmFsIFN1bQ%3D%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L-k6sgGoF9k&pp=ygUjMTU3Mi4gTWF0cml4IERpYWdvbmFsIFN1bWphdmFzY3JpcHQ%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/matrix-diagonal-sum/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/matrix-diagonal-sum/solutions/939505/javascript-simple-solution-using-two-pointers-with-explanation-o-n/\\\">- Algorithm: Iterative Diagonal Sum Calculation</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>```javascript<br/>const diagonalSum = mat => {<br/>    let sum = 0; // Sum of diagonal elements<br/>    let j; // Counter for secondary diagonal<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>```javascript<br/>const diagonalSum = mat => {<br/>  let sum = 0;<br/>  let j = mat[0].length - 1;</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize a variable `sum` to store the sum of diagonal elements.<br/>2. Iterate through each row `i` of the matrix.<br/>3. For the primary diagonal, add `mat[i][i]` to `sum`.<br/>4. For the secondary diagonal, calculate the column index as `j = mat.length - 1 - i` and add `mat[i][j]` to `sum` if `i` is not equal to `j` (to avoid double-counting the center element in odd-sized matrices).<br/>5. Return the final `sum`.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution involves a single loop through the matrix, adding up elements from both the primary and secondary diagonals, while ensuring that the center element of an odd-sized matrix is not double-counted.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n), where n is the number of rows (or columns) in the square matrix. This arises from the single pass through the matrix.</div>\"}",
