            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1684. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-the-number-of-consistent-strings\\\">1684. Count the Number of Consistent Strings</a></b></span>\\n<div>Count the number of strings in an array that consist only of characters from a given allowed string.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given a string `allowed` containing distinct characters and an array of strings `words`.<br/>2. A string is considered consistent if all its characters appear in `allowed`.<br/>3. Determine the number of consistent strings in `words`.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [allowed = \\\"ab\\\", words = [\\\"ad\\\",\\\"bd\\\",\\\"aaab\\\",\\\"baa\\\",\\\"badab\\\"]] => 2</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: allowed = \\\"ab\\\", words = [\\\"ad\\\",\\\"bd\\\",\\\"aaab\\\",\\\"baa\\\",\\\"badab\\\"]<br/>Output: 2<br/>Explanation: Strings \\\"aaab\\\" and \\\"baa\\\" are consistent since they only contain characters 'a' and 'b'.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: allowed = \\\"abc\\\", words = [\\\"a\\\",\\\"b\\\",\\\"c\\\",\\\"ab\\\",\\\"ac\\\",\\\"bc\\\",\\\"abc\\\"]<br/>Output: 7<br/>Explanation: All strings are consistent.<br/><br/><br/>Example 3:<br/><br/>Input: allowed = \\\"cad\\\", words = [\\\"cc\\\",\\\"acd\\\",\\\"b\\\",\\\"ba\\\",\\\"bac\\\",\\\"bad\\\",\\\"ac\\\",\\\"d\\\"]<br/>Output: 4<br/>Explanation: Strings \\\"cc\\\", \\\"acd\\\", \\\"ac\\\", and \\\"d\\\" are consistent.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= words.length <= 104<br/>1 <= allowed.length <= 26<br/>1 <= words[i].length <= 10<br/>The characters in allowed are distinct.<br/>words[i] and allowed contain only lowercase English letters.<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=og8SijKgPtY&pp=ygUsMTY4NC4gQ291bnQgdGhlIE51bWJlciBvZiBDb25zaXN0ZW50IFN0cmluZ3M%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=O9qU2jzAxgA&pp=ygU2MTY4NC4gQ291bnQgdGhlIE51bWJlciBvZiBDb25zaXN0ZW50IFN0cmluZ3NqYXZhc2NyaXB0\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-the-number-of-consistent-strings/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/count-the-number-of-consistent-strings/solutions/1013948/javascript-elegant-solution-using-a-set-and-reduce-with-explanation/\\\">- Algorithm: Set and Reduce</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>```javascript<br/>const countConsistentStrings = (allowed, words) => {<br/>    let set; // Set of allowed characters<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>const countConsistentStrings = (allowed, words) => {<br/>  let set = new Set(allowed);<br/>  return words.reduce((a, w) => {<br/>    return w.split('').every(l => set.has(l)) ? ++a : a;<br/>  }, 0);</div>\\n<div>1. Create a set `set` containing characters from `allowed`.<br/>2. Use `reduce` to iterate over `words`.<br/>3. For each word `w`, split it into characters.<br/>4. Check if every character `l` is present in `set`.<br/>5. If all characters are in `set`, increment the accumulator.<br/>6. Return the final count of consistent strings.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution uses a set to store allowed characters for quick lookup. It then iterates over each word, checking if every character is in the set. The `reduce` method accumulates the count of words that satisfy this condition.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n * m), where n is the number of words and m is the average length of each word. This is due to checking each character of each word against the set.</div>\"}",
