            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 804. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/unique-morse-code-words\\\">804. Unique Morse Code Words</a></b></span>\\n<div>Count the number of unique Morse code transformations for a given set of words.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Each English letter has a corresponding Morse code sequence.<br/>2. Given an array `words`, transform each word into its Morse code equivalent.<br/>3. Determine the number of unique Morse code transformations in the list.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [words = [\\\"gin\\\", \\\"zen\\\", \\\"gig\\\", \\\"msg\\\"]] => 2</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: words = [\\\"gin\\\",\\\"zen\\\",\\\"gig\\\",\\\"msg\\\"]<br/>Output: 2<br/>Explanation: The transformation of each word is:<br/>\\\"gin\\\" -> \\\"--...-.\\\"<br/>\\\"zen\\\" -> \\\"--...-.\\\"<br/>\\\"gig\\\" -> \\\"--...--.\\\"<br/>\\\"msg\\\" -> \\\"--...--.\\\"<br/>There are 2 different transformations: \\\"--...-.\\\" and \\\"--...--.\\\".<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: words = [\\\"a\\\"]<br/>Output: 1<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1 <= words.length <= 100<br/>1 <= words[i].length <= 12<br/>words[i] consists of lowercase English letters.<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WG_Hmo5eZro&pp=ygUcODA0LiBVbmlxdWUgTW9yc2UgQ29kZSBXb3Jkcw%3D%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RK21CkARysA&pp=ygUmODA0LiBVbmlxdWUgTW9yc2UgQ29kZSBXb3Jkc2phdmFzY3JpcHQ%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/unique-morse-code-words/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/unique-morse-code-words/solutions/329303/javascript-one-line-solution-w-explanation-52-ms-beats-94/\\\">- Algorithm: Mapping and Set Usage</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>```javascript<br/>const alphabet = {<br/>    // Morse code mapping for each letter<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>```javascript<br/>const alphabet = {<br/>    a: '.-', b: '-...',   c: '-.-.', d: '-..', e: '.', f: '..-.', g: '--.', h: '....', i: '..',  j: '.---',  k: '-.-',  l: '.-..', m: '--',<br/>    n: '-.',  o: '---', p: '.--.',  q: '--.-',  r: '.-.', s: '...', t: '-', u: '..-', v: '...-', w: '.--', x: '-..-',  y: '-.--', z: '--..'</div>\\n<div>1. Define a mapping of each letter to its Morse code equivalent.<br/>2. Iterate through each word in `words`.<br/>3. For each word, transform it into Morse code by replacing each letter with its Morse code.<br/>4. Use a set to store these transformations, ensuring uniqueness.<br/>5. Return the size of the set, which represents the number of unique Morse code transformations.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution leverages a map for Morse code transformations and a set to count unique Morse code strings derived from each word. This approach efficiently counts unique transformations without needing to compare each transformation manually.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n * m), where n is the number of words and m is the average length of each word. This arises from iterating over each letter of each word once.</div>\"}",
