            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1913. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-product-difference-between-two-pairs\\\">1913. Maximum Product Difference Between Two Pairs</a></b></span>\\n<div>Maximize the product difference between two pairs of elements in an array.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given an integer array `nums`.<br/>2. Choose four distinct indices `w`, `x`, `y`, and `z` such that the product difference between `(nums[w], nums[x])` and `(nums[y], nums[z])` is maximized.<br/>3. The product difference is defined as `(nums[w] * nums[x]) - (nums[y] * nums[z])`.<br/>4. Return the maximum product difference.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [nums = [5,6,2,7,4]] => 34</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [5,6,2,7,4]<br/>Output: 34<br/>Explanation: We can choose indices 1 and 3 for the first pair (6, 7) and indices 2 and 4 for the second pair (2, 4).<br/>The product difference is (6 * 7) - (2 * 4) = 34.<br/><br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: nums = [4,2,5,9,7,4,8]<br/>Output: 64<br/>Explanation: We can choose indices 3 and 6 for the first pair (9, 8) and indices 1 and 5 for the second pair (2, 4).<br/>The product difference is (9 * 8) - (2 * 4) = 64.<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>4 <= nums.length <= 104<br/>1 <= nums[i] <= 104<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vnBbIt2XPJw&pp=ygUyMTkxMy4gTWF4aW11bSBQcm9kdWN0IERpZmZlcmVuY2UgQmV0d2VlbiBUd28gUGFpcnM%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tFEK53Ils0I&pp=ygU8MTkxMy4gTWF4aW11bSBQcm9kdWN0IERpZmZlcmVuY2UgQmV0d2VlbiBUd28gUGFpcnNqYXZhc2NyaXB0\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-product-difference-between-two-pairs/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-product-difference-between-two-pairs/solutions/1732572/in-case-you-need-short-js-solution/\\\">- Algorithm: Sorting and Product Calculation</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>var maxProductDifference = function(nums) {<br/>    // Sort the array<br/>    // Calculate product difference between the largest and smallest pairs<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>var maxProductDifference = function(nums) {<br/>    nums.sort((a, b) => a - b);<br/>    return nums.slice(nums.length - 2).reduce((a, b) => a * b, 1) - nums.slice(0, 2).reduce((a, b) => a * b, 1);</div>\\n<div>1. Sort the array `nums` in ascending order.<br/>2. Calculate the product of the two largest elements (last two elements in the sorted array).<br/>3. Calculate the product of the two smallest elements (first two elements in the sorted array).<br/>4. Subtract the smaller product from the larger one.<br/>5. Return the result as the maximum product difference.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution involves sorting the array to easily access the largest and smallest pairs. The maximum product difference is obtained by subtracting the product of the two smallest elements from the product of the two largest elements.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n log n), where n is the number of elements in `nums`. This is due to the sorting step.</div>\"}",
