            "question": "{\"content\":\"<style>\\n    /* 1266. */\\n    .text-container {\\n      cursor: pointer;\\n      max-width: 20px;\\n      white-space: normal; /* Allow the text to wrap */\\n      overflow: hidden;\\n      position: relative;\\n      line-height: 1.4; /* Adjust for better readability */\\n      transition: max-width 0.3s ease-in-out, max-height 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition for expanding */\\n      max-height: 1.4em; /* Set to line height to show only the first line */\\n    }\\n    .text-container::after {\\n      content: '  ...  ';\\n      position: absolute;\\n      right: 0;\\n      bottom: 0;\\n      color: #d5d5d5;\\n      background:  #f0f0f0;\\n      width: 100%;\\n      text-align: right;\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover {\\n      max-width: 350px; /* Adjust as needed for hover */\\n      max-height: none; /* Allow it to expand to fit content */\\n    }\\n    .text-container:hover::after {\\n      display: none; /* Hide the ellipsis on hover */\\n    }\\n    a:link, a:visited {\\n        color: black;\\n    }\\n    resize-img. {\\n        max-height:450px;\\n        min-width:350px;\\n        width:auto;\\n        display:block;\\n        margin:auto;\\n        background-color: #131516;\\n    }\\n  </style>\\n<span><b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-time-visiting-all-points\\\">1266. Minimum Time Visiting All Points</a></b></span>\\n<div>Calculate the minimum time to visit all points on a 2D plane in the given order.<img src=\\\"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2019/11/14/1626_example_1.PNG\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" class=\\\"resize-img\\\"></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>1. Given an array of points with integer coordinates.<br/>2. Each movement (vertical, horizontal, diagonal) takes 1 second.<br/>3. Find the minimum time to travel through all points in the given sequence.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>- [points = [[1,1],[3,4],[-1,0]]] => 7</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>Example 1:<br/><br/>Input: points = [[1,1],[3,4],[-1,0]]<br/>Output: 7<br/>Explanation: One optimal path is [1,1] -> [2,2] -> [3,3] -> [3,4] -> [2,3] -> [1,2] -> [0,1] -> [-1,0]   <br/>Time from [1,1] to [3,4] = 3 seconds <br/>Time from [3,4] to [-1,0] = 4 seconds<br/>Total time = 7 seconds<br/><br/>Example 2:<br/><br/>Input: points = [[3,2],[-2,2]]<br/>Output: 5<br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>points.length == n<br/>1 <= n <= 100<br/>points[i].length == 2<br/>-1000 <= points[i][0], points[i][1] <= 1000<br/></div>\\n<span>\\n<a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xKnKFV1HbdI&pp=ygUmMTI2Ni4gTWluaW11bSBUaW1lIFZpc2l0aW5nIEFsbCBQb2ludHM%3D\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nJS: <a href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IcgZ_q2XNWU&pp=ygUwMTI2Ni4gTWluaW11bSBUaW1lIFZpc2l0aW5nIEFsbCBQb2ludHNqYXZhc2NyaXB0\\\"><svg xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\" x=\\\"0px\\\" y=\\\"0px\\\" width=\\\"30\\\" height=\\\"25\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 48 48\\\">\\n<path fill=\\\"#FF3D00\\\" d=\\\"M43.2,33.9c-0.4,2.1-2.1,3.7-4.2,4c-3.3,0.5-8.8,1.1-15,1.1c-6.1,0-11.6-0.6-15-1.1c-2.1-0.3-3.8-1.9-4.2-4C4.4,31.6,4,28.2,4,24c0-4.2,0.4-7.6,0.8-9.9c0.4-2.1,2.1-3.7,4.2-4C12.3,9.6,17.8,9,24,9c6.2,0,11.6,0.6,15,1.1c2.1,0.3,3.8,1.9,4.2,4c0.4,2.3,0.9,5.7,0.9,9.9C44,28.2,43.6,31.6,43.2,33.9z\\\"></path><path fill=\\\"#FFF\\\" d=\\\"M20 31L20 17 32 24z\\\"></path>\\n</svg></a>\\nSolutions:<a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-time-visiting-all-points/solutions/\\\">[1]</a></span>\"}",
            "answer": "{\"content\":\"<b><a href=\\\"https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-time-visiting-all-points/solutions/439924/javascript-easy-to-understand/\\\">- Algorithm: Iterative Point Distance Calculation</a></b>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>```javascript<br/>const minTimeToVisitAllPoints = points => {<br/>    let times = 0; // Total time to travel<br/><br/></div>\\n<div>const minTimeToVisitAllPoints = points => {<br/>  let times = 0;<br/>  for (let i = 1; i ＜ points.length; ++i) {<br/>    const p0 = points[i - 1];<br/>    const p1 = points[i];<br/>    times += Math.max(Math.abs(p1[0] - p0[0]), Math.abs(p1[1] - p0[1]));<br/>  return times;<br/>};</div>\\n<div>1. Initialize a variable `times` to keep track of the total time.<br/>2. Iterate over the array of points.<br/>3. For each pair of consecutive points, calculate the maximum of the absolute differences in x and y coordinates.<br/>4. Add this value to `times`, representing the time taken to move between these points.<br/>5. Return the total time `times` after completing the iteration.</div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The solution calculates the time to move between each pair of consecutive points. The time is the maximum of the horizontal and vertical distances, which accounts for diagonal movement as well.<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/></br></br>No 'Shorter/Alternative Solution' section found<br/><br/></div>\\n<div class=\\\"text-container\\\"><br/>The time complexity is O(n), where n is the number of points. This is due to iterating through the array once.</div>\"}",
